  restocking), CombatController, PromptController (themed prompts), Lib.Movement, the players'
  11 clips, the Pocket Pistol (v2: the grip rakes back) and the Wrench. Before it, Landon's
  answers to the Prompt 9 and 10 questions: the biggest draw goes dark first, wrecked rooms draw
  nothing, the founders start idle, idle residents use the Lounge.
* **Landon's Prompt 11 answers (2026-11-08)**: carried ammo per player, the hotbar, a Heal
  button (Medkits over 1.5 s; H, hold D-pad up, a touch button) with Medkits restocked at the
  Medbay, throwables thrown with Fire (`ThrowItem`: Frag, Flare, Foam, Shock Mine), no
  regeneration, and a melee weapon in every kit (new: Defib Paddles, Antenna Whip, Hazard Hook,
  Hunting Knife, Power Wrench). The aim fixed: the clips' wrists, and the waist follows the aim.
* **Prompt 12 (2026-11-08)**: threats and monsters (Run). Rules.Threat, ThreatDirector,
  BreachService, MonsterService, the residents' flee and swat, ThreatController, monsters in
  NPCAnimator, the A4 Mines monsters and their clips. Then the A4 detail pass (Landon: more
  detailed monsters, scary bosses): the four monsters rebuilt (the Tunnel Hound gained a Jaw
  bone, the Spitter Grub four mouth petals), the Brood Mother with seven clips and her egg sac,
  generator meta written as model attributes.
* **Prompt 13 (2026-11-08 and 9)**: disasters and repairs (Run). Rules.Disasters,
  Rules.Modifiers, DisasterService (fires, blackouts and the fuse box, cave-ins with
  Lib.Hazards, the Reactor meltdown and its valves, electrical surges, the Surge's disaster),
  DisasterController, wrecked rooms and repairs (the Welder, residents), trapped residents,
  monsters skipping blocked targets, tools in WeaponService, the HUD's Meltdown telegram; art:
  the Extinguisher, the Welder, doorway and tunnel rubble and two hotbar icons.
* **Prompt 14 (2026-11-09)**: digging, depth bands, Disturbance and Push Deeper (Run).
  Rules.Dig, Rules.Loot, DigService (dig prompts, stacking, the roll: ore pockets, cave
  openings, caches, nests; Push Deeper votes, the Drill Bay's queue, Disturbance and its extra
  breach and Tremor), DigController, the HUD's seismograph, the camera shake, the Command View's
  dig notes and queue; ThreatDirector bursts; art: the Drill, the Pickaxe, the nest, the cave
  mouth and two hotbar icons.
]=]
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item></Item></Item><Item class="Folder" referent="RBX0000006F"><Properties><string name="Name">StarterPlayerScripts</string></Properties><Item class="LocalScript" referent="RBX0000005D"><Properties><string name="Name">ClientBootstrap</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ClientBootstrap: the only LocalScript (bible Section 23). It loads every controller in
	the Controllers folder beside it, runs every Init in dependency order and then every
	Start, waits for the server to be ready and tells it the client is ready (ClientReady),
	which makes the server send the replication snapshot.

	Never add another LocalScript: write a controller (see Documentation.ARCHITECTURE).
]]

local began = os.clock()

local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Utilities = Shared:WaitForChild("Utilities")
local Loader = require(Utilities:WaitForChild("Loader"))
local Log = require(Utilities:WaitForChild("Log"))
local Remotes = require(Shared:WaitForChild("Remotes"))

local SERVER_WAIT_SECONDS = 30

local log = Log.new("ClientBootstrap")

local controllers = Loader.Collect(script.Parent:WaitForChild("Controllers"), "Controller")
local report = Loader.Run(controllers, log)

local waited = 0
while ReplicatedStorage:GetAttribute("ServerReady") ~= true and waited < SERVER_WAIT_SECONDS do
	waited += task.wait(0.1)
end
if ReplicatedStorage:GetAttribute("ServerReady") ~= true then
	log:Warn("the server isn't ready after %d s; continuing", SERVER_WAIT_SECONDS)
end

Remotes.FireServer("ClientReady")
log:Info(
	"client ready: %d controllers (%s) in %.1f ms",
	#report.Order,
	table.concat(report.Order, ", "),
	(os.clock() - began) * 1000
)
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="Folder" referent="RBX00000069"><Properties><string name="Name">Controllers</string></Properties><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000005F"><Properties><string name="Name">CameraController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	CameraController: the over-the-shoulder camera (bible Sections 9 and 26: "wall fade and zoom
	caps built and tested in prompt 5, before anything depends on them").

	* Over the right shoulder by default; SwapShoulder (V, the right stick click, the HUD's
	  Shoulder button) moves it to the other side in ShoulderSwapSeconds.
	* Aim (right mouse, the left trigger, the HUD's Aim button; Run place only) narrows the
	  field of view from 70 to 50 (Tuning.Player.AimFieldOfView), brings the camera in to
	  AimDistance, slows walking to AimWalkSpeed (Lib.Movement) and turns the character to where
	  the camera looks. Face(reason, on) turns it the same way without aiming (firing from the
	  hip, a swing; Prompt 11), and Nudge(yaw, pitch) turns the camera a little (recoil, aim
	  assist). Shake(seconds, degrees) shakes it (Prompt 14: a Tremor).
	* Zoom (the wheel, a pinch) between Distance.Min and Distance.Max, capped at IndoorMax while
	  the character is in a bunker cell.
	* Zoom caps: a spherecast from the shoulder keeps the camera out of walls, slabs and rock: it
	  pulls in at once and eases back out. In a bunker cell the camera also stays between the
	  floor and the ceiling panels, sliding in along its view (Shafts are open overhead).
	* Wall fade: front walls (FrontWall tag) and furniture (CameraFade tag) never stop the
	  camera; when they stand between the camera and the character, or touch the camera, they
	  fade (Lib.Fade, this client only). So the camera can stand outside a room's open front.
	  Characters and anything tagged CameraIgnore are passed through.
	* The local character fades as the camera comes within CharacterFadeDistance of the head.
	* PC: the mouse is locked to the centre with the cursor hidden and the Reticle shown; any
	  controller frees the cursor with FreeCursor(reason, true) (menus, the Command View).
	* Other views take the camera with Suspend(reason) and give it back with Resume(reason).
	* Fallback: if the update errors ErrorsBeforeFallback times in a row, the controller stops
	  and hands the camera to Roblox's default camera, which the places set to Invisicam
	  (StarterPlayer.DevCameraOcclusionMode).
]]

local CollectionService = game:GetService("CollectionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local CameraRig = require(Shared.Rules.CameraRig)
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local Fade = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("Fade"))
local Movement = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("Movement"))

local log = Log.new("CameraController")

local FRONT_WALL_TAG = "FrontWall"
local FADE_TAG = "CameraFade"
local IGNORE_TAG = "CameraIgnore"
local FADE_SOURCE = "Camera"
local RENDER_NAME = "100Y_Camera"
local RENDER_PRIORITY = Enum.RenderPriority.Camera.Value + 1
local MAX_FADE_HITS = 4
local PIVOT_LAG = 2 -- the smoothed pivot never trails the head by more than this (studs)

local CameraController = {
	Name = "CameraController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "ReplicaController" },
	ShoulderChanged = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<number>,
	AimChanged = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<boolean>,
}

local input: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local t: { [string]: any } = {}
local aimFieldOfView = 50
local inRun = false

local yaw = 0
local pitch = 0
local side = 1 -- 1: right shoulder, -1: left
local sideBlend = 1
local aiming = false
local aimBlend = 0
local wanted = 9 -- the zoom the player chose
local distance = 9 -- the camera's distance this frame
local pivotY: number? = nil
local sensitivity = 1
local suspended: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local cursorFree: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local errors = 0
local stopped = false
local wasActive = false
local faded: { [BasePart]: boolean } = {}
local characterFade = 0
local fadedCharacter: Model? = nil
local walkHumanoid: Humanoid? = nil
local slowed = false
local turned = false
local facers: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local reticle: { Gui: ScreenGui, Hip: GuiObject?, Aim: GuiObject? }? = nil
local lastFrame = { Distance = 0, Blocked = false, Indoors = false, Fading = 0, Position = Vector3.zero }

local blockParams = RaycastParams.new()
blockParams.FilterType = Enum.RaycastFilterType.Exclude
blockParams.IgnoreWater = true
local fadeParams = RaycastParams.new()
fadeParams.FilterType = Enum.RaycastFilterType.Include
fadeParams.IgnoreWater = true
local nearParams = OverlapParams.new()
nearParams.FilterType = Enum.RaycastFilterType.Include
local filtersDirty = true

-- Filters ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The camera passes through characters, CameraIgnore, CameraFade and front walls; it fades
-- the last two.
local function rebuildFilters()
	filtersDirty = false
	local passThrough: { Instance } = {}
	local fadeable: { Instance } = {}
	for _, player in Players:GetPlayers() do
		if player.Character then
			table.insert(passThrough, player.Character)
		end
	end
	for _, item in CollectionService:GetTagged(IGNORE_TAG) do
		table.insert(passThrough, item)
	end
	for _, tag in { FADE_TAG, FRONT_WALL_TAG } do
		for _, item in CollectionService:GetTagged(tag) do
			table.insert(passThrough, item)
			table.insert(fadeable, item)
		end
	end
	blockParams.FilterDescendantsInstances = passThrough
	fadeParams.FilterDescendantsInstances = fadeable
	nearParams.FilterDescendantsInstances = fadeable
end

local function markDirty()
	filtersDirty = true
end

-- Fading -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A front wall fades as a whole piece; anything else fades alone.
local function fadeGroup(part: BasePart, into: { [BasePart]: number }, amount: number)
	if CollectionService:HasTag(part, FRONT_WALL_TAG) then
		local parent = part.Parent
		if parent and parent:IsA("Model") then
			for _, sibling in parent:GetChildren() do
				if sibling:IsA("BasePart") and CollectionService:HasTag(sibling, FRONT_WALL_TAG) then
					into[sibling] = math.max(into[sibling] or 0, t.FrontWallTransparency)
				end
			end
		end
		into[part] = math.max(into[part] or 0, t.FrontWallTransparency)
		return
	end
	into[part] = math.max(into[part] or 0, amount)
end

-- Fadeable parts on the lines from the camera to points on the character.
local function occluders(from: Vector3, targets: { Vector3 }, into: { [BasePart]: number })
	for _, target in targets do
		local origin = from
		for _ = 1, MAX_FADE_HITS do
			local delta = target - origin
			if delta.Magnitude < 0.05 then
				break
			end
			local hit = workspace:Raycast(origin, delta, fadeParams)
			if not hit then
				break
			end
			local part = hit.Instance
			if part:IsA("BasePart") then
				fadeGroup(part, into, t.FadeTransparency)
			end
			origin = hit.Position + delta.Unit * 0.05
		end
	end
end

local function applyFades(now: { [BasePart]: number })
	for part in faded do
		if now[part] == nil then
			Fade.Clear(part, FADE_SOURCE)
			faded[part] = nil
		end
	end
	for part, amount in now do
		Fade.Set(part, FADE_SOURCE, amount)
		faded[part] = true
	end
end

local function clearFades()
	Fade.ClearSource(FADE_SOURCE)
	table.clear(faded)
end

local function fadeCharacter(character: Model?, amount: number)
	if character ~= fadedCharacter then
		characterFade = -1
		fadedCharacter = character
	end
	if not character or math.abs(amount - characterFade) < 0.01 then
		return
	end
	characterFade = amount
	for _, item in character:GetDescendants() do
		if item:IsA("BasePart") or item:IsA("Decal") then
			local target: any = item
			target.LocalTransparencyModifier = amount
		end
	end
end

-- Mouse, reticle, walking --------------------------------------------------------------------

local function active(): boolean
	return not stopped and next(suspended) == nil
end

-- Shake (Prompt 14: a Tremor): a small turn that fades over the seconds given.
local shakeUntil, shakeSeconds, shakeDegrees = 0, 0, 0

local function shakeOffset(): CFrame
	local left = shakeUntil - os.clock()
	if left <= 0 then
		return CFrame.identity
	end
	local k = shakeDegrees * (left / math.max(shakeSeconds, 0.01))
	local t = os.clock() * 31
	return CFrame.Angles(math.rad(math.noise(t, 0.5) * k * 2), math.rad(math.noise(t, 7.5) * k * 2), 0)
end

local function updateMouse()
	local locked = active() and next(cursorFree) == nil and input:Device() ~= "Touch" and not GuiService.MenuIsOpen
	local behavior = if locked then Enum.MouseBehavior.LockCenter else Enum.MouseBehavior.Default
	if UserInputService.MouseBehavior ~= behavior then
		UserInputService.MouseBehavior = behavior
	end
	if UserInputService.MouseIconEnabled == locked then
		UserInputService.MouseIconEnabled = not locked
	end
end

local function findReticle()
	local playerGui = Players.LocalPlayer:FindFirstChildOfClass("PlayerGui")
	local gui = playerGui and playerGui:FindFirstChild("Reticle")
	if gui and gui:IsA("ScreenGui") then
		local hip = gui:FindFirstChild("Hip", true)
		local aim = gui:FindFirstChild("Aim", true)
		reticle = {
			Gui = gui,
			Hip = if hip and hip:IsA("GuiObject") then hip else nil,
			Aim = if aim and aim:IsA("GuiObject") then aim else nil,
		}
	else
		reticle = nil
	end
end

local function updateReticle()
	local current = reticle
	if not current or current.Gui.Parent == nil then
		findReticle()
		current = reticle
	end
	if not current then
		return
	end
	local show = active() and next(cursorFree) == nil
	if current.Gui.Enabled ~= show then
		current.Gui.Enabled = show
	end
	local aimed = aimBlend >= 0.5
	if current.Hip and current.Hip.Visible ~= (inRun and not aimed) then
		current.Hip.Visible = inRun and not aimed
	end
	if current.Aim and current.Aim.Visible ~= (inRun and aimed) then
		current.Aim.Visible = inRun and aimed
	end
end

-- Aiming slows walking (Lib.Movement); aiming and Face() turn the character with the camera.
local function updateWalking(humanoid: Humanoid, root: BasePart)
	if humanoid ~= walkHumanoid then
		walkHumanoid = humanoid
		slowed = false
		turned = false
		Movement.Apply()
	end
	if aiming ~= slowed then
		slowed = aiming
		Movement.Set("Aim", if aiming then t.AimWalkSpeed else nil)
	end
	local facing = aiming or next(facers) ~= nil
	if facing ~= turned then
		turned = facing
		humanoid.AutoRotate = not facing
	end
	if facing then
		root.CFrame = CFrame.new(root.Position) * CFrame.Angles(0, yaw, 0)
	end
end

local function releaseWalking()
	local humanoid = walkHumanoid
	if humanoid and turned and humanoid.Parent then
		humanoid.AutoRotate = true
	end
	Movement.Set("Aim", nil)
	slowed = false
	turned = false
end

-- Is the cell at this point a Shaft (open overhead for the stair)?
local function inShaft(point: Vector3): boolean
	local floor, column = Grid.CellAt(point)
	if not floor or not column then
		return false
	end
	local cell = replica:Get("Cells", Grid.Key(floor, column))
	local roomId = if type(cell) == "table" then cell.Room else nil
	local room = if type(roomId) == "string" then replica:Get("Rooms", roomId) else nil
	return type(room) == "table" and room.Type == "Shaft"
end

-- The frame ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function step(dt: number)
	updateMouse()
	updateReticle()
	if not active() then
		if wasActive then
			wasActive = false
			clearFades()
			releaseWalking()
			fadeCharacter(fadedCharacter, 0)
		end
		input:TakeLook(dt)
		input:TakeZoom()
		return
	end
	wasActive = true
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	local root = humanoid and humanoid.RootPart
	if not camera or not character or not humanoid or not root then
		input:TakeLook(dt)
		input:TakeZoom()
		return
	end
	if camera.CameraType ~= Enum.CameraType.Scriptable then
		camera.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Scriptable
	end
	if filtersDirty then
		rebuildFilters()
	end

	-- Look, shoulder and aim
	local turn = input:TakeLook(dt) * sensitivity * (1 + (t.AimSensitivity - 1) * aimBlend)
	yaw -= math.rad(turn.X)
	pitch = CameraRig.ClampPitch(pitch - math.rad(turn.Y))
	sideBlend = CameraRig.MoveToward(sideBlend, side, dt * 2 / math.max(t.ShoulderSwapSeconds, 1e-3))
	aimBlend = CameraRig.MoveToward(aimBlend, if aiming then 1 else 0, dt / math.max(t.AimBlendSeconds, 1e-3))

	-- The pivot: head height, its height smoothed a little (stairs)
	local head = root.Position + Vector3.new(0, t.PivotHeight, 0)
	local smoothY = if pivotY then CameraRig.Approach(pivotY, head.Y, t.PivotFollowPerSecond, dt) else head.Y
	pivotY = math.clamp(smoothY, head.Y - PIVOT_LAG, head.Y + PIVOT_LAG)
	local pivot = Vector3.new(head.X, pivotY :: number, head.Z)

	-- Indoors: the bunker cell the character is in
	local low: number?, high: number? = nil, nil
	if inRun then
		low, high = CameraRig.CellHeights(pivot)
	end
	local indoors = low ~= nil
	if indoors and inShaft(pivot) then
		high = nil -- the Shaft is open overhead (the stair goes up through it)
	end

	-- Zoom
	local nearest, farthest = CameraRig.ZoomRange(indoors)
	local zoomInput = input:TakeZoom()
	if zoomInput ~= 0 then
		wanted = math.clamp(math.min(wanted, farthest) + zoomInput, nearest, if indoors then farthest else t.Distance.Max)
	end
	local zoomGoal = math.clamp(wanted, nearest, farthest)
	local goal = zoomGoal + (math.min(t.AimDistance, zoomGoal) - zoomGoal) * aimBlend

	-- The focus beside the head, kept out of a wall the character stands against
	local shoulder = t.ShoulderOffset * (1 + (t.AimShoulder - 1) * aimBlend)
	local focus = CameraRig.Focus(pivot, yaw, sideBlend, shoulder, t.ShoulderRaise)
	local toFocus = focus - pivot
	if toFocus.Magnitude > 1e-3 then
		local hit = workspace:Spherecast(pivot, t.CollisionRadius * 0.75, toFocus, blockParams)
		if hit then
			focus = pivot + toFocus.Unit * math.max(0, hit.Distance - t.WallMargin)
		end
	end

	-- How far back the camera can go: walls and rock, then the cell's floor and ceiling
	local rotation = CameraRig.Rotation(yaw, pitch)
	local look = rotation.LookVector
	local allowed = goal
	local blocked = false
	local hit = workspace:Spherecast(focus, t.CollisionRadius, -look * goal, blockParams)
	if hit then
		allowed = math.max(t.NearestDistance, hit.Distance - t.WallMargin)
		blocked = true
	end
	if indoors then
		local limit = CameraRig.HeightLimit(focus, look, low :: number, high or math.huge)
		if limit < allowed then
			allowed = math.max(t.NearestDistance, limit)
			blocked = true
		end
	end
	if allowed < distance then
		distance = allowed -- pull in at once
	else
		distance = CameraRig.Approach(distance, allowed, t.EaseOutPerSecond, dt)
	end

	local position = focus - look * distance
	camera.CFrame = CFrame.new(position) * rotation * shakeOffset()
	camera.Focus = CFrame.new(focus)
	camera.FieldOfView = t.FieldOfView + (aimFieldOfView - t.FieldOfView) * aimBlend

	-- Wall fade: between the camera and the character, and touching the camera
	local fades: { [BasePart]: number } = {}
	occluders(position, { head, root.Position, focus }, fades)
	for _, part in workspace:GetPartBoundsInRadius(position, t.NearFadeRadius, nearParams) do
		fadeGroup(part, fades, 1)
	end
	applyFades(fades)

	-- The character fades when the camera is at its head
	local gap = (position - head).Magnitude
	local closeness = math.clamp((t.CharacterFadeDistance - gap) / (t.CharacterFadeDistance * 0.5), 0, 1)
	fadeCharacter(character, closeness)

	updateWalking(humanoid, root)

	lastFrame.Distance = distance
	lastFrame.Blocked = blocked
	lastFrame.Indoors = indoors
	lastFrame.Fading = Fade.Count(FADE_SOURCE)
	lastFrame.Position = position
end

local function onRender(dt: number)
	if stopped then
		return
	end
	local ok, err = pcall(step, dt)
	if ok then
		errors = 0
		return
	end
	errors += 1
	log:Warn("camera update failed (%d): %s", errors, tostring(err))
	if errors >= t.ErrorsBeforeFallback then
		stopped = true
		clearFades()
		releaseWalking()
		local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
		if camera then
			camera.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Custom
			camera.FieldOfView = t.FieldOfView
		end
		UserInputService.MouseBehavior = Enum.MouseBehavior.Default
		UserInputService.MouseIconEnabled = true
		log:Error("the over-the-shoulder camera stopped; Roblox's camera (Invisicam) takes over")
	end
end

-- API ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CameraController:SwapShoulder()
	side = -side
	CameraController.ShoulderChanged:Fire(side)
end

function CameraController:SetShoulder(value: number)
	local wantedSide = if value < 0 then -1 else 1
	if wantedSide ~= side then
		CameraController:SwapShoulder()
	end
end

function CameraController:SetAiming(on: boolean)
	local value = on and inRun and active() and next(cursorFree) == nil
	if value == aiming then
		return
	end
	aiming = value
	CameraController.AimChanged:Fire(value)
end

function CameraController:IsAiming(): boolean
	return aiming
end

-- Turn the character to where the camera looks while `reason` holds (firing from the hip, a
-- melee swing), without aiming's zoom.
function CameraController:Face(reason: string, on: boolean)
	facers[reason] = if on then true else nil
end

-- Turn the camera by a few degrees (recoil kicks it up; aim assist pulls it toward a target).
-- Shake the over-the-shoulder camera for `seconds`, up to `degrees` (Prompt 14: Tremors).
function CameraController:Shake(seconds: number, degrees: number)
	shakeUntil = os.clock() + seconds
	shakeSeconds = seconds
	shakeDegrees = degrees
end

function CameraController:Nudge(yawDegrees: number, pitchDegrees: number)
	yaw += math.rad(yawDegrees)
	pitch = CameraRig.ClampPitch(pitch + math.rad(pitchDegrees))
end

-- Where the camera looks, as a ray from the camera (what the reticle covers).
function CameraController:AimRay(): Ray?
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	if not camera then
		return nil
	end
	local size = camera.ViewportSize
	return camera:ViewportPointToRay(size.X / 2, size.Y / 2)
end

-- Point the camera (degrees): yaw 0 looks toward -Z, pitch below 0 looks down.
function CameraController:SetLook(yawDegrees: number, pitchDegrees: number)
	yaw = math.rad(yawDegrees)
	pitch = CameraRig.ClampPitch(math.rad(pitchDegrees))
end

function CameraController:SetZoom(studs: number)
	wanted = math.clamp(studs, t.Distance.Min, t.Distance.Max)
end

-- A sensitivity multiplier from the player's settings (Settings screen, later).
function CameraController:SetSensitivity(value: number)
	sensitivity = math.clamp(value, 0.1, 4)
end

-- Another view takes the camera (the Command View, a cutscene) until Resume(reason).
function CameraController:Suspend(reason: string)
	suspended[reason] = true
end

function CameraController:Resume(reason: string)
	suspended[reason] = nil
end

-- A menu frees the mouse cursor while it is open.
function CameraController:FreeCursor(reason: string, on: boolean)
	cursorFree[reason] = if on then true else nil
end

function CameraController:State(): { [string]: any }
	return {
		Active = active(),
		Stopped = stopped,
		Yaw = math.deg(yaw) % 360,
		Pitch = math.deg(pitch),
		Shoulder = if side > 0 then "right" else "left",
		Aiming = aiming,
		Wanted = wanted,
		Distance = lastFrame.Distance,
		Blocked = lastFrame.Blocked,
		Indoors = lastFrame.Indoors,
		Fading = lastFrame.Fading,
		Position = lastFrame.Position,
		FieldOfView = if workspace.CurrentCamera then workspace.CurrentCamera.FieldOfView else 0,
		Device = input:Device(),
		Suspended = next(suspended) ~= nil,
		CursorFree = next(cursorFree) ~= nil,
	}
end

-- Lifecycle ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CameraController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	t = CameraRig.Tuning()
	aimFieldOfView = Config.Get("Tuning", "Player").AimFieldOfView[2]
	inRun = Constants.PlaceKind() == "Run"
	pitch = math.rad(t.StartPitch)
	wanted = t.Distance.Default
	distance = wanted
	Fade.SetSeconds(t.FadeSeconds)
end

function CameraController:Start()
	input:On("SwapShoulder", function()
		CameraController:SwapShoulder()
	end)
	input:On("Aim", function()
		CameraController:SetAiming(true)
	end, function()
		CameraController:SetAiming(false)
	end)

	for _, tag in { FADE_TAG, FRONT_WALL_TAG, IGNORE_TAG } do
		CollectionService:GetInstanceAddedSignal(tag):Connect(markDirty)
		CollectionService:GetInstanceRemovedSignal(tag):Connect(markDirty)
	end
	local function watch(player: Player)
		player.CharacterAdded:Connect(markDirty)
		player.CharacterRemoving:Connect(markDirty)
	end
	for _, player in Players:GetPlayers() do
		watch(player)
	end
	Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(watch)
	Players.PlayerRemoving:Connect(markDirty)

	-- A new character looks the way it spawned facing
	local function faceSpawn(character: Model)
		local root = character:WaitForChild("HumanoidRootPart", 10)
		if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then
			local lookVector = root.CFrame.LookVector
			yaw = math.atan2(-lookVector.X, -lookVector.Z)
			pitch = math.rad(t.StartPitch)
			pivotY = nil
			distance = math.min(wanted, select(2, CameraRig.ZoomRange(inRun)))
		end
		aiming = false
		aimBlend = 0
	end
	Players.LocalPlayer.CharacterAdded:Connect(faceSpawn)
	if Players.LocalPlayer.Character then
		task.spawn(faceSpawn, Players.LocalPlayer.Character)
	end

	RunService:BindToRenderStep(RENDER_NAME, RENDER_PRIORITY, onRender)
	log:Debug("over-the-shoulder camera on (%s)", if inRun then "Run" else "Lobby")
end

return CameraController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000060"><Properties><string name="Name">CommandViewController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	CommandViewController: the Command View (bible Section 7), a flat side view of the whole
	bunker that any player opens with one button, anywhere, while the character stays in the
	world and can be hit. Run place only.

	* Open and close: the CommandView action (Tab, the console's View button, the HUD button).
	  It is The Frame in docked mode (Section 18): top bar, tab rail and detail panel, with the
	  live bunker in zone C (the page Cabinet.Pages.CommandView, built in Studio).
	* Camera: far away with a narrow field of view, looking at the bunker's front, so it reads
	  nearly flat. It opens centred on the character with a 0.3 s move and moves back over the
	  shoulder on close. Front walls fade out (Lib.Fade, source "CommandView") and the lighting
	  lifts a little so the rock reads. The character's controls are off while it's open.
	* Moving the view: drag (mouse or one finger), WASD or the arrow keys, the left stick; zoom
	  with the wheel, a pinch or the right stick.
	* Picking: click or tap a cell; on a gamepad, A picks the cell under the centre mark. The
	  detail panel shows a room (level, cells, condition, power, output; actions: upgrade, merge,
	  tear down), an open cell (the build menu: every room type with its cost, or why it's
	  locked) or rock (whether it can be dug, its band and ore).
	* Proposals go through handlers the votes set (SetHandler: "Build", "Upgrade", "Merge",
	  "TearDown"; Prompt 8). Without a handler the main action stays greyed out.
	* Overlays (tabs Power, Morale, Threat, Production) colour the room labels' lamps from
	  providers later systems register (SetOverlay); without one they read "no readings yet".
	* Ping: the footer's Ping button or the Ping key (G, the D-pad's up) pings the selected cell
	  (the PingCell remote); every player sees it here and on the mini-map.
	* Taking damage while the view is open flashes the screen edge red.

	* Status (Section 7: every room shows status icons: dark, wrecked, burning, flooded):
	  providers later systems register (SetStatus) give a room's lamp and reading ("ON FIRE")
	  whenever the overlay tab has nothing to say about it; a condition note (SetConditionNote)
	  adds to the room panel's Condition (Prompt 13).

	API for later prompts: SetHandler(action, fn(choice)), SetOverlay(name, provider),
	SetStatus(name, provider), SetConditionNote(fn), SetCellNotes(fn), SetRockOptions(fn) and
	Refresh() (Prompt 14: digging), ShowGhost(id, floor, column, span, label)
	and HideGhost(id) for open votes, Blink(key, on) for alerts, Select(floor, column), IsOpen(),
	State().
]]

local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local Lighting = game:GetService("Lighting")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")
local CollectionService = game:GetService("CollectionService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Bunker = require(Shared.Rules.Bunker)
local CV = require(Shared.Rules.CommandView)
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Construction = require(Shared.Rules.Construction)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local UIContract = require(Shared.UIContract)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local Fade = require(Lib:WaitForChild("Fade"))
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))

local log = Log.new("CommandViewController")

export type Choice = {
	Action: string, -- "Build", "Upgrade", "Merge", "TearDown"; "Assign", "Unassign", "AutoAssign", "MarkDig", "UnmarkDig" (no vote)
	Floor: number,
	Column: number,
	RoomType: string?, -- Build
	RoomId: string?, -- Upgrade, Merge, TearDown, Assign
	Other: string?, -- Merge: the room it joins
	Level: number?, -- Upgrade: the new level
	ResidentId: string?, -- Assign, Unassign
	Label: string?, -- Assign, Unassign: the main action's words
}
export type Overlay = (roomId: string, room: any) -> (string?, string?) -- lamp sprite, legend text

local SCREEN = "CommandView"
local FADE_SOURCE = "CommandView"
local FRONT_WALL_TAG = "FrontWall"
local RENDER_NAME = "100Y_CommandView"
local RENDER_PRIORITY = Enum.RenderPriority.Camera.Value - 1 -- before CameraController drains zoom input
local PING_ACTION = "100Y_CVPing"
local PICK_ACTION = "100Y_CVPick"
local HOLD_ACTION = "100Y_CVHold"
local TABS = {
	{ Id = "Build", Label = "Build", Icon = "Icon_Grid" },
	{ Id = "Power", Label = "Power", Icon = "Icon_Power" },
	{ Id = "Morale", Label = "Morale", Icon = "Icon_Check" },
	{ Id = "Threat", Label = "Threat", Icon = "Icon_Shield" },
	{ Id = "Production", Label = "Production", Icon = "Icon_Scrap" },
}
local OVERLAY_TEXT: { [string]: string } = { -- bible Section 7's overlays
	Power = "Green: lit. Red: dark for want of power. Rooms go dark farthest from the Reactor Core or a Generator first.",
	Morale = "Each room's workers' average morale. Green: Happy or better. Amber: Settled. Red: Unhappy or worse.",
	Threat = "Likely breach points.",
	Production = "What each room makes a cycle. Amber: no one works there. Red: dark or wrecked.",
}
local PAN_KEYS: { [Enum.KeyCode]: Vector2 } = {
	[Enum.KeyCode.W] = Vector2.new(0, 1),
	[Enum.KeyCode.Up] = Vector2.new(0, 1),
	[Enum.KeyCode.S] = Vector2.new(0, -1),
	[Enum.KeyCode.Down] = Vector2.new(0, -1),
	[Enum.KeyCode.A] = Vector2.new(-1, 0),
	[Enum.KeyCode.Left] = Vector2.new(-1, 0),
	[Enum.KeyCode.D] = Vector2.new(1, 0),
	[Enum.KeyCode.Right] = Vector2.new(1, 0),
}
local CREAM = Color3.fromHex("#F2E6C9")
local RUST = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B")

local CommandViewController = {
	Name = "CommandViewController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "CameraController", "UIController", "ReplicaController", "HUDController" },
	Opened = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<()>,
	Closed = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<()>,
	Selected = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<number?, number?>,
}

local input: any = nil
local cameraController: any = nil
local ui: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local inRun = false

local t: { [string]: any } = {}
local open = false
local center = Vector2.zero -- the view's centre: world X and Y
local height = 60 -- studs of the bunker that fit the view's height
local gridZ = 0
local bounds: CV.Bounds = { Left = 0, Right = 0, Top = 0, Bottom = 0 }
local moving: { Alpha: number, From: CFrame, FromFov: number, To: (() -> (CFrame, number))?, Back: boolean, Done: (() -> ())? }? = nil
local before: { CFrame: CFrame, FieldOfView: number }? = nil
local lightingBefore: { [string]: any }? = nil
local selected: { number }? = nil
local choice: Choice? = nil
local tab = "Build"
local bunker: any = nil
local bunkerDirty = true
local labels: { [string]: any } = {}
local labelsDirty = true
local ghosts: { [string]: { Frame: any, Floor: number, Column: number, Span: number } } = {}
local pings: { { Frame: any, Floor: number, Column: number, Until: number } } = {}
local blinking: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local handlers: { [string]: (Choice) -> () } = {}
local overlays: { [string]: Overlay } = {}
local statuses: { [string]: Overlay } = {} -- Prompt 13: a room's status lamp when the overlay is silent
local conditionNote: ((string) -> string?)? = nil
-- Prompt 14: what digging says about a cell, and the dig queue's actions on rock
export type CellNote = { Title: string, Text: string }
export type CellOption = { Name: string, Value: string, Choice: Choice? }
local cellNotes: ((floor: number, column: number, state: string) -> { CellNote })? = nil
local rockOptions: ((floor: number, column: number) -> { CellOption })? = nil
local selectionMark: any = nil
local drag: { Start: Vector2, Last: Vector2, Moved: boolean, Touch: InputObject? }? = nil
local pinch: { [InputObject]: Vector2 } = {}
local lastHealth: number? = nil
local frontWalls: { [BasePart]: boolean } = {}
local connections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}

-- Layout --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function gui(): ScreenGui?
	return ui:Gui()
end

local function part(path: string): any
	local root = gui()
	assert(root, "CommandViewController: no Frame")
	local found = UIContract.Find(root, path)
	assert(found, `CommandViewController: Frame.{path} is missing (see Shared.UIContract)`)
	return found
end

local function page(): any
	return part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView")
end

local function clone(template: string): any
	local copy = part("Templates." .. template):Clone()
	copy.Visible = true
	return copy
end

local function clear(container: Instance)
	for _, child in container:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			child:Destroy()
		end
	end
end

-- Screen and world ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Zone C's rectangle in viewport pixels (GUI coordinates plus the top inset).
local function viewRect(): (Vector2, Vector2)
	local view = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View")
	local inset = GuiService:GetGuiInset()
	return view.AbsolutePosition + inset, view.AbsoluteSize
end

local function inView(point: Vector2): boolean
	local origin, size = viewRect()
	return point.X >= origin.X and point.Y >= origin.Y and point.X <= origin.X + size.X and point.Y <= origin.Y + size.Y
end

-- The camera for the current centre and zoom: far away along +Z, looking at the bunker's front,
-- shifted so the centre shows in the middle of zone C rather than the middle of the screen.
local function viewCFrame(): (CFrame, number)
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local distance, fieldOfView = CV.Lens(height)
	local viewport = camera.ViewportSize
	local origin, size = viewRect()
	local zoneCentre = origin + size / 2
	local offset = zoneCentre - viewport / 2
	local perPixel = height / math.max(viewport.Y, 1)
	local position = Vector3.new(center.X - offset.X * perPixel, center.Y + offset.Y * perPixel, gridZ + distance)
	return CFrame.lookAt(position, position - Vector3.zAxis), fieldOfView
end

-- The cell under a viewport point: the ray meets the plane of the cells' centres.
local function cellAt(point: Vector2): (number?, number?)
	local ray = workspace.CurrentCamera:ViewportPointToRay(point.X, point.Y)
	if math.abs(ray.Direction.Z) < 1e-6 then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local along = (gridZ - ray.Origin.Z) / ray.Direction.Z
	if along <= 0 then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local floor, column = Grid.CellAt(ray.Origin + ray.Direction * along)
	if floor and column and Grid.OnGrid(floor, column) then
		return floor, column
	end
	return nil, nil
end

-- Cells from column to column + span - 1 on a floor (their interiors, floor to ceiling) in
-- zone C's scale.
local function cellRect(floor: number, column: number, span: number): (UDim2, UDim2, boolean)
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local low, high = CV.CellBox(floor, column, span)
	local a = camera:WorldToViewportPoint(Vector3.new(low.X, high.Y, gridZ))
	local b = camera:WorldToViewportPoint(Vector3.new(high.X, low.Y, gridZ))
	local origin, size = viewRect()
	local x0, y0 = (math.min(a.X, b.X) - origin.X) / size.X, (math.min(a.Y, b.Y) - origin.Y) / size.Y
	local x1, y1 = (math.max(a.X, b.X) - origin.X) / size.X, (math.max(a.Y, b.Y) - origin.Y) / size.Y
	local visible = x1 > 0 and y1 > 0 and x0 < 1 and y0 < 1
	return UDim2.fromScale(x0, y0), UDim2.fromScale(x1 - x0, y1 - y0), visible
end

-- A world point in zone C's scale.
local function pointIn(world: Vector3): (UDim2, boolean)
	local p = workspace.CurrentCamera:WorldToViewportPoint(world)
	local origin, size = viewRect()
	local x, y = (p.X - origin.X) / size.X, (p.Y - origin.Y) / size.Y
	return UDim2.fromScale(x, y), x >= 0 and y >= 0 and x <= 1 and y <= 1
end

-- The bunker -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function currentBunker(): any
	if bunkerDirty or not bunker then
		bunker = Bunker.FromSnapshot(replica:All("Cells"), replica:All("Rooms"))
		bunkerDirty = false
	end
	return bunker
end

local function context(): CV.Context
	local era = table.find(Config.Ids("Eras"), RunState.Get("Era") or "") or 1
	local unlocked = {}
	for roomType in replica:All("Unlocked") do
		unlocked[roomType] = true
	end
	return { Era = era, Deepest = currentBunker():DeepestFloor(), Unlocked = unlocked }
end

-- The stockpile as EconomyService replicates it (RunState, one value per resource).
local function stockNow(): { [string]: number }
	local stock = {}
	for _, id in Config.Ids("Resources") do
		if RunState.Fields[id] then
			local value = RunState.Get(id)
			if type(value) == "number" then
				stock[id] = value
			end
		end
	end
	return stock
end

local function covers(thing: any, floor: number, column: number): boolean
	return type(thing) == "table" and thing.Floor == floor and type(thing.Column) == "number"
		and column >= thing.Column and column < thing.Column + (thing.Span or 1)
end

-- The construction site on a cell (BuildService's Sites collection), if any.
local function siteAt(floor: number, column: number): any
	for _, site in replica:All("Sites") do
		if covers(site, floor, column) then
			return site
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- The open vote (live or waiting) whose proposal covers a cell, if any.
local function voteAt(floor: number, column: number): any
	for _, vote in replica:All("Votes") do
		if type(vote) == "table" and (vote.Status == "Live" or vote.Status == "Queued") and covers(vote.Subject, floor, column) then
			return vote
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- "120 SCRAP" when the stockpile can pay, else "120 SCRAP · 40 SHORT", and whether it can.
local function costLine(costs: { [string]: number }): (string, boolean)
	local ok, short, missing = Construction.CanAfford(costs, stockNow())
	if ok or not short then
		return CV.CostText(costs), true
	end
	return `{CV.CostText(costs)}  ·  {missing} {string.upper(Config.Get("Resources", short).Name)} SHORT`, false
end

local function roomName(roomType: string): string
	local info = Config.Find("Rooms", roomType)
	return if info then info.Name else roomType
end

-- Labels, marks and pings ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The overlay's lamp and reading for a room ("+8 FOOD", "DARK"), when an overlay tab is on.
local function overlayLamp(roomId: string, room: any): (string?, string?)
	if tab == "Build" then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local provider = overlays[tab]
	if not provider then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local ok, lamp, reading = pcall(provider, roomId, room)
	if ok then
		return lamp, reading
	end
	return nil, nil
end

local function rebuildLabels()
	labelsDirty = false
	local holder = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Labels")
	clear(holder)
	table.clear(labels)
	for id, room in replica:All("Rooms") do
		local label = clone("RoomLabel")
		label.Name = id
		label:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = `{string.upper(roomName(room.Type))}  ·  L{room.Level}`
		label.Parent = holder
		labels[id] = label
	end
end

local function placeLabels()
	for id, label in labels do
		local room = replica:Get("Rooms", id)
		if room then
			-- just under the room's ceiling (the label hangs from its top edge)
			local low, high = CV.CellBox(room.Floor, room.Column, room.Span)
			local top = Vector3.new((low.X + high.X) / 2, high.Y - 1, gridZ)
			local position, visible = pointIn(top)
			label.Position = position
			label.Visible = visible
			label.ImageColor3 = if blinking[id] then RUST else Color3.new(1, 1, 1)
			local lamp = label:FindFirstChild("Lamp")
			local sprite, reading = overlayLamp(id, room)
			if sprite == nil and reading == nil then
				for _, provider in statuses do
					local ok, s, r = pcall(provider, id, room)
					if ok and (s or r) then
						sprite, reading = s, r
						break
					end
				end
			end
			lamp.Visible = sprite ~= nil
			if sprite then
				KitRuntime.SetSprite(lamp, sprite)
			end
			local chip = label:FindFirstChild("Reading") -- Prompt 9's patch adds it
			if chip then
				chip.Visible = reading ~= nil and visible
				if reading then
					chip.Text.Text = reading
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

local function placeMarks()
	if selectionMark then
		local floor, column, span = selected and selected[1], selected and selected[2], 1
		if selected and floor and column then
			local roomId = currentBunker():UnitAt(floor, column)
			local room = roomId and currentBunker():Room(roomId)
			if room then
				column, span = room.Column, room.Span
			end
			local position, size, visible = cellRect(floor, column, span)
			selectionMark.Position = position
			selectionMark.Size = size
			selectionMark.Visible = visible
		else
			selectionMark.Visible = false
		end
	end
	for _, ghost in ghosts do
		local position, size, visible = cellRect(ghost.Floor, ghost.Column, ghost.Span)
		ghost.Frame.Position = position
		ghost.Frame.Size = size
		ghost.Frame.Visible = visible
	end
	local now = os.clock()
	for i = #pings, 1, -1 do
		local ping = pings[i]
		if now > ping.Until then
			ping.Frame:Destroy()
			table.remove(pings, i)
		else
			-- the pin's tip at the middle of the cell's interior
			local low, high = CV.CellBox(ping.Floor, ping.Column, 1)
			local position, visible = pointIn(Vector3.new((low.X + high.X) / 2, (low.Y + high.Y) / 2, gridZ))
			ping.Frame.Position = position
			ping.Frame.Visible = visible
		end
	end
end

-- The detail panel ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "there is already one" -> "There is already one" (Rules.Bunker's reasons are lower case)
local function sentence(text: string): string
	return (string.gsub(text, "^%l", string.upper))
end

local function section(order: number, label: string, body: string)
	local s = ui:Clone("Section")
	s.LayoutOrder = order
	s:FindFirstChild("Label").Text = string.upper(label)
	s:FindFirstChild("Body").Text = body
	s.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail.Body")
end

local rowConnections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}
local refreshDetail: () -> ()

local function optionRow(order: number, name: string, value: string, enabled: boolean, pick: Choice?)
	local row = clone("OptionRow")
	row.LayoutOrder = order
	row:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(name)
	row:FindFirstChild("Value").Text = value
	row.ImageTransparency = if enabled then 0 else 0.35
	local lamp = row:FindFirstChild("Lamp")
	local isChosen = pick ~= nil and choice ~= nil and choice.Action == pick.Action and choice.RoomType == pick.RoomType
		and choice.Other == pick.Other and choice.RoomId == pick.RoomId and choice.ResidentId == pick.ResidentId
	KitRuntime.SetSprite(lamp, if isChosen then "Lamp_Orange" else "Lamp_Off")
	lamp.Visible = pick ~= nil
	if pick and enabled then
		table.insert(rowConnections, row.Activated:Connect(function()
			choice = pick
			refreshDetail()
		end))
	end
	row.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail.Options")
end

local function setMainAction()
	local current = choice
	if not current then
		ui:SetMainAction(nil)
		return
	end
	-- jobs are never voted on (Section 8): the choice applies at once
	if current.Action == "Assign" or current.Action == "Unassign" or current.Action == "AutoAssign" then
		ui:SetMainAction({
			Label = current.Label or "Assign",
			Enabled = true,
			OnPress = function()
				if current.Action == "AutoAssign" then
					Remotes.FireServer("AutoAssign")
				else
					Remotes.FireServer("AssignResident", current.ResidentId or "", if current.Action == "Assign" then current.RoomId or "" else "")
				end
				choice = nil
				refreshDetail()
			end,
		})
		return
	end
	-- the Drill Bay's dig queue is never voted on (Section 7; Prompt 14)
	if current.Action == "MarkDig" or current.Action == "UnmarkDig" then
		local handler = handlers[current.Action]
		ui:SetMainAction({
			Label = current.Label or (if current.Action == "MarkDig" then "Queue for the Drill Bay" else "Take off the queue"),
			Enabled = handler ~= nil,
			OnPress = function()
				local h = handlers[current.Action]
				if h then
					h(current)
				end
				choice = nil
				refreshDetail()
			end,
		})
		return
	end
	-- solo runs have no votes (Section 8, rule 6): the choice applies at once
	local verb = if (RunState.Get("ReadyNeeded") or 1) <= 1 then
		(if current.Action == "Build" then "Build" elseif current.Action == "Upgrade" then "Upgrade to" elseif current.Action == "Merge" then "Merge" else "Tear down")
		else "Propose"
	local label = if current.Action == "Build" then `{verb} {roomName(current.RoomType or "")}`
		elseif current.Action == "Upgrade" then (if verb == "Propose" then `Propose level {current.Level}` else `Upgrade to level {current.Level}`)
		elseif current.Action == "Merge" then (if verb == "Propose" then "Propose merge" else "Merge")
		else (if verb == "Propose" then "Propose teardown" else "Tear down")
	local handler = handlers[current.Action]
	ui:SetMainAction({
		Label = label,
		Enabled = handler ~= nil,
		OnPress = function()
			local h = handlers[current.Action]
			if h then
				h(current)
				-- proposed: the panel shows the proposal once the vote replicates
				choice = nil
				refreshDetail()
			end
		end,
	})
end

-- What a room's power reading says (PowerService's Power collection).
local function powerLine(roomId: string, room: any, info: any): string
	local power = replica:Get("Power", roomId)
	if info.PowerOutput then
		local made = if power then power.Made or 0 else 0
		return if made > 0 then `Makes {math.floor(made + 0.5)} with its crew. Every room draws from it.`
			else "Makes nothing: no one works here. Without power the rooms farthest from it go dark first."
	end
	local draw = info.Power[room.Level] * room.Span
	if draw <= 0 then
		return "Draws none."
	end
	if power and power.Dark then
		return `Dark: draws {draw}, but there isn't enough power. Dark rooms make nothing.`
	end
	return `Draws {draw}. Lit.`
end

local OUTPUT_WORDS: { [string]: string } = {
	Research = "Lab research", Morale = "morale", Recruits = "recruits", Training = "training",
	Crafting = "crafting", Thawing = "thawing", Decon = "decon", Digging = "digging",
}

-- What a room's output reading says (EconomyService's Production collection), or nil.
local function outputLine(roomId: string): string?
	local made = replica:Get("Production", roomId)
	if type(made) ~= "table" then
		return nil
	end
	local resource = Config.Find("Resources", made.Makes or "")
	local what = if resource then resource.Name else (OUTPUT_WORDS[made.Makes] or tostring(made.Makes))
	if made.Idle == "Wrecked" then
		return `Makes {what}; nothing until it is repaired.`
	elseif made.Idle == "Dark" then
		return `Makes {what}; nothing while it is dark.`
	elseif made.Idle == "NoCrew" then
		return `Makes {what} once residents work here.`
	end
	return `{made.Rate} {what} a cycle, {made.Workers} working.`
end

local function showRoom(roomId: string)
	local b = currentBunker()
	local room = b:Room(roomId) :: any
	local info = Config.Get("Rooms", room.Type)
	local detail = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail")
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(info.Name)
	detail:FindFirstChild("Sub").Text = `LEVEL {room.Level}  ·  {room.Span} CELL{if room.Span > 1 then "S" else ""}  ·  FLOOR {room.Floor}`
	local condition = if room.Wrecked
		then `Wrecked: {room.HP} of {room.MaxHP} HP. Works again at {Bunker.RepairedAt(room.MaxHP)}.`
		else `{room.HP} of {room.MaxHP} HP`
	if conditionNote then
		local ok, note = pcall(conditionNote, roomId)
		if ok and note then
			condition ..= `\n{note}`
		end
	end
	section(1, "Condition", condition)
	section(2, "Power", powerLine(roomId, room, info))
	local output = outputLine(roomId)
	if output then
		section(3, "Output", output)
	end
	section(4, "What it does", info.Text)
	-- an upgrade being built (Nightmare): the room works at its old level until it's done
	local site = siteAt(room.Floor, room.Column)
	if site and site.Kind == "Upgrade" then
		section(5, "Upgrading", `To level {site.Level}: {math.floor((site.Progress or 0) * 100)}% done. `
			.. (if (site.Helpers or 0) > 0 then `{site.Helpers} helping.` else "Stand in it to build faster."))
	end
	-- a proposal already open on this room: no second one until it closes (Section 8)
	local openVote = voteAt(room.Floor, room.Column) or (if site and site.Kind == "Upgrade" then site else nil)
	if openVote and openVote ~= site then
		section(6, "Proposal open", `{openVote.ProposerName}: {openVote.Title}. Vote on the banner.`)
	end
	local order = 1
	if room.Level < 3 then
		local nextLevel = room.Level + 1
		local costs = Construction.CostsAt(room.Type, nextLevel, room.Span)
		local value, affordable = costLine(costs)
		local research = Construction.ResearchFor(room.Type, nextLevel)
		local have = RunState.Get("Research") or 0
		local enabled = affordable and have >= research and not openVote
		if research > 0 then
			value = if affordable and have < research then `Needs {research} Lab research ({math.floor(have)} so far)`
				else `{value}  ·  {research} LAB RESEARCH`
		end
		optionRow(order, `Upgrade to level {nextLevel}`, value, enabled,
			if enabled then { Action = "Upgrade", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId, Level = nextLevel } else nil)
		order += 1
	end
	for _, column in { room.Column - 1, room.Column + room.Span } do
		local otherId = b:UnitAt(room.Floor, column)
		local other = otherId and b:Room(otherId)
		if other and other.Id ~= roomId then
			local ok, why = b:CanMerge(roomId, other.Id)
			if ok or other.Type == room.Type then
				local can = ok and not openVote and not voteAt(other.Floor, other.Column)
				optionRow(order, `Merge with the {roomName(other.Type)}`, if ok then `{room.Span + other.Span} cells together` else sentence(why or ""), can,
					if can then { Action = "Merge", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId, Other = other.Id } else nil)
				order += 1
			end
		end
	end
	local canRemove, why = b:CanRemove(roomId)
	local can = canRemove and not openVote
	local refund = Construction.Refund(room.Type, room.Level, room.Span)
	local gives = if next(refund) then `{Construction.CostText(refund)} BACK` else "Its cells become open cells again"
	optionRow(order, "Tear down", if canRemove then gives else sentence(why or ""), can,
		if can then { Action = "TearDown", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId } else nil)
	order += 1
	-- jobs (Prompt 10): who works here, and who could
	local stat = info.WorkerStat
	if stat then
		local slots = Config.Get("Tuning", "Rooms").WorkerSlotsPerCell[room.Level] * room.Span
		local workers, idle = {}, {}
		for id, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
			if type(resident) == "table" and resident.State == "Alive" then
				if resident.Job == roomId then
					table.insert(workers, { Id = id, R = resident })
				elseif resident.Job == nil then
					table.insert(idle, { Id = id, R = resident })
				end
			end
		end
		local function byStat(a: any, b: any): boolean
			local sa, sb = a.R.Stats[stat] or 0, b.R.Stats[stat] or 0
			if sa ~= sb then
				return sa > sb
			end
			return a.Id < b.Id
		end
		table.sort(workers, byStat)
		table.sort(idle, byStat)
		local names = {}
		for _, w in workers do
			table.insert(names, `{w.R.Name} ({stat} {w.R.Stats[stat]}, {w.R.Mood})`)
		end
		section(7, `Workers  ·  {#workers} of {slots}`, if #names > 0 then table.concat(names, "; ") .. "."
			else `Nobody works here yet. The job uses {stat}.`)
		local full = #workers >= slots
		for i, entry in idle do
			if i > 6 then
				break
			end
			local first = entry.R.First or entry.R.Name
			optionRow(order, `Assign {entry.R.Name}`, if full then "The room is full" else `{stat} {entry.R.Stats[stat]}  ·  {entry.R.Mood}`,
				not full, if not full then { Action = "Assign", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId,
					ResidentId = entry.Id, Label = `Assign {first}` } else nil)
			order += 1
		end
		for _, w in workers do
			local first = w.R.First or w.R.Name
			optionRow(order, `Take {w.R.Name} off the job`, "They go idle until you assign them again", true,
				{ Action = "Unassign", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId, ResidentId = w.Id,
					Label = `Take {first} off` })
			order += 1
		end
		if #idle > 0 then
			optionRow(order, "Auto-Assign", `{#idle} idle: fill empty jobs by best stat`, true,
				{ Action = "AutoAssign", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId, Label = "Auto-Assign" })
		end
	end
end

local function showOpenCell(floor: number, column: number)
	local detail = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail")
	detail:FindFirstChild("Sub").Text = `FLOOR {floor}  ·  COLUMN {column}  ·  {string.upper(Grid.BandOf(floor).Name)}`
	local site = siteAt(floor, column)
	if site then
		detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "UNDER CONSTRUCTION"
		section(1, "Building", `A {roomName(site.Type)}: {math.floor((site.Progress or 0) * 100)}% built.`)
		section(2, "Help", if (site.Helpers or 0) > 0
			then `{site.Helpers} helping; each one builds it 25% faster.`
			else "Stand in the cell to build it faster.")
		return
	end
	local vote = voteAt(floor, column)
	if vote then
		detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "PROPOSED"
		section(1, "Vote", `{vote.ProposerName}: {vote.Title}. Vote on the banner.`)
		return
	end
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "OPEN CELL"
	section(1, "Build here", "Pick a room type, then propose it to the team.")
	local notes = if cellNotes then cellNotes(floor, column, "Dug") else {}
	for i, note in notes do
		section(1 + i, note.Title, note.Text)
	end
	local b = currentBunker()
	local ctx = context()
	local available, locked = {}, {}
	for _, roomType in Config.Ids("Rooms") do
		-- Fixed rooms (the Blast Door, the Reactor Core) come with the bunker and are never built
		if not Config.Get("Rooms", roomType).Fixed then
			local ok, why = CV.RoomChoice(b, roomType, floor, column, ctx)
			table.insert(if ok then available else locked, { Type = roomType, Why = why })
		end
	end
	local order = 1
	for _, entry in available do
		local info = Config.Get("Rooms", entry.Type)
		local value, affordable = costLine(Construction.CostsAt(entry.Type, 1))
		optionRow(order, info.Name, value, affordable,
			if affordable then { Action = "Build", Floor = floor, Column = column, RoomType = entry.Type } else nil)
		order += 1
	end
	for _, entry in locked do
		optionRow(order, Config.Get("Rooms", entry.Type).Name, sentence(entry.Why or ""), false, nil)
		order += 1
	end
end

local function showRock(floor: number, column: number)
	local detail = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail")
	local band = Grid.BandOf(floor)
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "ROCK"
	detail:FindFirstChild("Sub").Text = `FLOOR {floor}  ·  COLUMN {column}  ·  {string.upper(band.Name)}`
	local b = currentBunker()
	local ok, why = b:CanDig(floor, column)
	section(1, "Digging", if ok then "Can be dug: it is beside or under a dug cell or room." else `Can't be dug yet: {why}.`)
	if band.Ore then
		section(2, "Ore", `{Config.Get("Resources", band.Ore).Name} in the {band.Name}.`)
	end
	if Grid.IsBandStart(floor) and floor > b:DeepestFloor() then
		section(3, "Next band", `The first cell of the {band.Name}: opening it needs a Push Deeper vote.`)
	end
	local notes = if cellNotes then cellNotes(floor, column, "Rock") else {}
	for i, note in notes do
		section(3 + i, note.Title, note.Text)
	end
	local options = if rockOptions then rockOptions(floor, column) else {}
	for i, option in options do
		optionRow(i, option.Name, option.Value, option.Choice ~= nil, option.Choice)
	end
end

local function showNothing()
	local detail = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail")
	local b = currentBunker()
	local rooms, open = 0, 0
	for _ in replica:All("Rooms") do
		rooms += 1
	end
	for _, cell in replica:All("Cells") do
		if type(cell) == "table" and cell.Room == nil then
			open += 1
		end
	end
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "BUNKER SECTION"
	detail:FindFirstChild("Sub").Text = `{rooms} ROOMS  ·  {open} OPEN CELL{if open == 1 then "" else "S"}  ·  DEPTH {b:DeepestFloor()}`
	section(1, "Pick a cell", "A room to upgrade, merge or tear down, an open cell to build on, or rock to dig.")
end

local function showOverlayLegend()
	local text = OVERLAY_TEXT[tab]
	if not text then
		return
	end
	-- at the top of the detail panel, above whatever is selected
	section(0, `{tab} overlay`, if overlays[tab] then text else `{text} No readings yet.`)
end

local lastRefreshed: string? = nil -- the selection the panel last showed

refreshDetail = function()
	if not open then
		return
	end
	-- a refresh of the same selection (a vote's tally, a site's progress) keeps the menu's scroll
	local options = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail.Options")
	local key = if selected then Grid.Key(selected[1], selected[2]) else ""
	local scroll = if key == lastRefreshed then options.CanvasPosition else Vector2.zero
	lastRefreshed = key
	for _, connection in rowConnections do
		connection:Disconnect()
	end
	table.clear(rowConnections)
	clear(part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail.Body"))
	clear(options)
	local cell = selected
	if not cell then
		choice = nil
		showNothing()
	else
		local state, roomId = currentBunker():State(cell[1], cell[2])
		if state == "Room" and roomId then
			showRoom(roomId)
		elseif state == "Dug" then
			showOpenCell(cell[1], cell[2])
		else
			-- a rock cell's only choices are the dig queue's (Prompt 14); keep one picked for this cell
			local keep = choice ~= nil and (choice.Action == "MarkDig" or choice.Action == "UnmarkDig")
				and choice.Floor == cell[1] and choice.Column == cell[2]
			if not keep then
				choice = nil
			end
			showRock(cell[1], cell[2])
		end
	end
	showOverlayLegend()
	setMainAction()
	if scroll ~= Vector2.zero then
		task.defer(function()
			options.CanvasPosition = scroll -- after the list layout has sized the canvas again
		end)
	end
end

-- Selecting and pinging -------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CommandViewController:Select(floor: number?, column: number?)
	if floor and column and Grid.OnGrid(floor, column) then
		local same = selected ~= nil and selected[1] == floor and selected[2] == column
		selected = { floor, column }
		if not same then
			choice = nil
		end
	else
		selected = nil
		choice = nil
	end
	refreshDetail()
	CommandViewController.Selected:Fire(floor, column)
end

local function pingSelected()
	if selected and Remotes.InPlace("PingCell") then
		Remotes.FireServer("PingCell", selected[1], selected[2])
	end
end

local function onPinged(floor: number, column: number)
	if not open or type(floor) ~= "number" or type(column) ~= "number" then
		return
	end
	local mark = clone("PingMark")
	mark.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Marks")
	table.insert(pings, { Frame = mark, Floor = floor, Column = column, Until = os.clock() + Config.Get("Tuning", "Ping").Seconds })
end

-- Moving the camera -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function panBy(world: Vector2)
	center = CV.Clamp(center + world, bounds)
end

local function zoomBy(factor: number)
	local pitch = Grid.Pitch()
	height = math.clamp(height * factor, t.MinFloors * pitch.Y, t.MaxFloors * pitch.Y)
end

local function readInput(dt: number)
	-- wheel and pinch (InputController gathers both; we take them before CameraController)
	local zoom = input:TakeZoom()
	if zoom ~= 0 then
		local step = Config.Get("Tuning", "Camera").ZoomStep
		zoomBy(1 + t.ZoomStep * zoom / step)
	end
	input:TakeLook(dt) -- one-finger drags arrive here too; the view pans from its own touch tracking
	local perSecond = height * t.PanFloorsPerSecond / t.StartFloors
	local move = Vector2.zero
	if not UserInputService:GetFocusedTextBox() then
		for key, direction in PAN_KEYS do
			if UserInputService:IsKeyDown(key) then
				move += direction
			end
		end
	end
	for _, state in UserInputService:GetGamepadState(Enum.UserInputType.Gamepad1) do
		if state.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick1 and state.Position.Magnitude > t.StickDeadzone then
			move += Vector2.new(state.Position.X, state.Position.Y)
		elseif state.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick2 and math.abs(state.Position.Y) > t.StickDeadzone then
			zoomBy(1 - state.Position.Y * dt * 1.5)
		end
	end
	if move.Magnitude > 0 then
		panBy(move.Unit * math.min(move.Magnitude, 1) * perSecond * dt)
	end
end

local function render(dt: number)
	if not open and not moving then
		return
	end
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	if open and not (moving and moving.Back) then
		readInput(dt)
	end
	local current = moving
	if current then
		current.Alpha = math.min(1, current.Alpha + dt / math.max(t.MoveSeconds, 0.01))
		local eased = TweenService:GetValue(current.Alpha, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.InOut)
		local toCFrame, toFov = (current.To :: any)()
		camera.CFrame = current.From:Lerp(toCFrame, eased)
		camera.FieldOfView = current.FromFov + (toFov - current.FromFov) * eased
		if current.Alpha >= 1 then
			moving = nil
			if current.Done then
				current.Done()
			end
		end
	else
		local cframe, fov = viewCFrame()
		camera.CFrame = cframe
		camera.FieldOfView = fov
	end
	if open then
		if labelsDirty then
			rebuildLabels()
		end
		placeLabels()
		placeMarks()
		local cursor = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Cursor")
		cursor.Visible = input:Device() == "Gamepad"
	end
end

-- Input handlers ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function onInputBegan(io: InputObject)
	if not open then
		return
	end
	if io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton1 then
		local point = UserInputService:GetMouseLocation()
		if inView(point) then
			drag = { Start = point, Last = point, Moved = false, Touch = nil }
		end
	elseif io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch then
		local point = Vector2.new(io.Position.X, io.Position.Y) + GuiService:GetGuiInset()
		if inView(point) then
			pinch[io] = point
			local count = 0
			for _ in pinch do
				count += 1
			end
			drag = if count == 1 then { Start = point, Last = point, Moved = false, Touch = io } else nil
		end
	end
end

local function onInputChanged(io: InputObject)
	if not open then
		return
	end
	local current = drag
	if io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseMovement and current and not current.Touch then
		local point = UserInputService:GetMouseLocation()
		local delta = point - current.Last
		current.Last = point
		if (point - current.Start).Magnitude > t.DragPixels then
			current.Moved = true
		end
		if current.Moved then
			local perPixel = height / math.max(workspace.CurrentCamera.ViewportSize.Y, 1)
			panBy(Vector2.new(-delta.X, delta.Y) * perPixel)
		end
	elseif io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch and pinch[io] then
		local point = Vector2.new(io.Position.X, io.Position.Y) + GuiService:GetGuiInset()
		pinch[io] = point
		if current and current.Touch == io then
			local delta = point - current.Last
			current.Last = point
			if (point - current.Start).Magnitude > t.DragPixels then
				current.Moved = true
			end
			if current.Moved then
				local perPixel = height / math.max(workspace.CurrentCamera.ViewportSize.Y, 1)
				panBy(Vector2.new(-delta.X, delta.Y) * perPixel)
			end
		end
	end
end

local function onInputEnded(io: InputObject)
	local current = drag
	if io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton1 and current and not current.Touch then
		drag = nil
		if open and not current.Moved then
			CommandViewController:Select(cellAt(current.Start))
		end
	elseif io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch then
		pinch[io] = nil
		if current and current.Touch == io then
			drag = nil
			if open and not current.Moved then
				CommandViewController:Select(cellAt(current.Start))
			end
		end
	end
end

-- Open and close ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The character stays where it was left: its movement keys and sticks are sunk while the view is
-- open (Roblox's PlayerModule isn't an instance in every place, so this goes through
-- ContextActionService rather than its controls object).
-- Roblox's touch thumbstick and jump button: hidden while the view is open, or a drag in zone C
-- could walk the character away (it stays where it was left, Section 7).
local touchControlsBefore: boolean? = nil

local function holdCharacter(on: boolean)
	if not on then
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(HOLD_ACTION)
		if touchControlsBefore ~= nil then
			GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled = touchControlsBefore
			touchControlsBefore = nil
		end
		return
	end
	if touchControlsBefore == nil then
		touchControlsBefore = GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled
	end
	GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled = false
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(HOLD_ACTION, function()
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 20,
		Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterForward, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterBackward,
		Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterLeft, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterRight, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterJump,
		Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick1, Enum.KeyCode.Space)
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	if humanoid then
		humanoid:Move(Vector3.zero)
	end
end

local function fadeFrontWalls(on: boolean)
	if on then
		for _, item in CollectionService:GetTagged(FRONT_WALL_TAG) do
			if item:IsA("BasePart") then
				Fade.Set(item, FADE_SOURCE, 1)
				frontWalls[item] = true
			end
		end
	else
		Fade.ClearSource(FADE_SOURCE)
		table.clear(frontWalls)
	end
end

local function liftLighting(on: boolean)
	if on then
		lightingBefore = {
			Ambient = Lighting.Ambient,
			OutdoorAmbient = Lighting.OutdoorAmbient,
			ExposureCompensation = Lighting.ExposureCompensation,
		}
		Lighting.Ambient = Color3.fromHex(t.Ambient)
		Lighting.OutdoorAmbient = Color3.fromHex(t.OutdoorAmbient)
		Lighting.ExposureCompensation = t.ExposureCompensation
	elseif lightingBefore then
		Lighting.Ambient = lightingBefore.Ambient
		Lighting.OutdoorAmbient = lightingBefore.OutdoorAmbient
		Lighting.ExposureCompensation = lightingBefore.ExposureCompensation
		lightingBefore = nil
	end
end

local function flashEdge()
	local edge = part("DamageEdge")
	edge.Visible = true
	for _, strip in edge:GetChildren() do
		if strip:IsA("Frame") then
			strip.BackgroundTransparency = 0
			TweenService:Create(strip, TweenInfo.new(0.6, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.Out), {
				BackgroundTransparency = 1,
			}):Play()
		end
	end
	task.delay(0.65, function()
		if edge.Parent then
			edge.Visible = false
		end
	end)
end

local function helpText(): string
	local device = input:Device()
	if device == "Gamepad" then
		return "LEFT STICK MOVE  ·  RIGHT STICK ZOOM  ·  A PICK  ·  D-PAD UP PING"
	elseif device == "Touch" then
		return "DRAG TO MOVE  ·  PINCH TO ZOOM  ·  TAP A CELL"
	end
	return "DRAG OR WASD TO MOVE  ·  SCROLL TO ZOOM  ·  CLICK A CELL  ·  G PING"
end

local function bindKeys(on: boolean)
	if not on then
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(PING_ACTION)
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(PICK_ACTION)
		return
	end
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(PING_ACTION, function(_, state)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			pingSelected()
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 20, Enum.KeyCode.G, Enum.KeyCode.DPadUp)
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(PICK_ACTION, function(_, state)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			local origin, size = viewRect()
			CommandViewController:Select(cellAt(origin + size / 2))
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 30, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonA)
end

local function onOpen(_page: Frame)
	open = true
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	before = { CFrame = camera.CFrame, FieldOfView = camera.FieldOfView }
	cameraController:Suspend(SCREEN)
	camera.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Scriptable
	holdCharacter(true)
	bounds = CV.Bounds()
	gridZ = Grid.CellPosition(1, 0).Z
	height = t.StartFloors * Grid.Pitch().Y
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	center = CV.Clamp(if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then Vector2.new(root.Position.X, root.Position.Y) else Vector2.zero, bounds)
	selected = nil
	choice = nil
	labelsDirty = true
	fadeFrontWalls(true)
	liftLighting(true)
	selectionMark = clone("CellMark")
	selectionMark.Visible = false
	selectionMark.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Marks")
	part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Help.Text").Text = helpText()
	ui:SetFooterActions({
		{ Label = "Ping", OnPress = pingSelected },
		{ Label = "Residents", OnPress = function()
			-- the roster (ResidentsController, Prompt 10); closing it comes back here
			if ui:IsRegistered("Residents") then
				ui:Open("Residents")
			end
		end },
	})
	bindKeys(true)
	GuiService.SelectedObject = nil
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	lastHealth = if humanoid then humanoid.Health else nil
	moving = { Alpha = 0, From = camera.CFrame, FromFov = camera.FieldOfView, To = viewCFrame, Back = false, Done = nil }
	refreshDetail()
	CommandViewController.Opened:Fire()
end

local function onClose()
	if not open then
		return
	end
	open = false
	bindKeys(false)
	drag = nil
	table.clear(pinch)
	for _, ping in pings do
		ping.Frame:Destroy()
	end
	table.clear(pings)
	if selectionMark then
		selectionMark:Destroy()
		selectionMark = nil
	end
	for _, connection in rowConnections do
		connection:Disconnect()
	end
	table.clear(rowConnections)
	fadeFrontWalls(false)
	liftLighting(false)
	holdCharacter(false)
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local back = before
	before = nil
	if back then
		local target = back
		moving = {
			Alpha = 0,
			From = camera.CFrame,
			FromFov = camera.FieldOfView,
			To = function()
				return target.CFrame, target.FieldOfView
			end,
			Back = true,
			Done = function()
				cameraController:Resume(SCREEN)
			end,
		}
	else
		cameraController:Resume(SCREEN)
	end
	CommandViewController.Closed:Fire()
end

-- API ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CommandViewController:Toggle()
	if not inRun or not ui:Gui() then
		return
	end
	if ui:Current() == SCREEN then
		ui:Close()
	elseif not ui:IsOpen() then
		ui:Open(SCREEN)
	end
end

function CommandViewController:IsOpen(): boolean
	return open
end

-- A proposal's handler: "Build", "Upgrade", "Merge" or "TearDown" (the votes, Prompt 8).
function CommandViewController:SetHandler(action: string, handler: ((Choice) -> ())?)
	handlers[action] = handler
	if open then
		setMainAction()
	end
end

-- An overlay's provider: (roomId, room) -> lamp sprite (Lamp_Green, Lamp_Amber, Lamp_Red...).
function CommandViewController:SetOverlay(name: string, provider: Overlay?)
	assert(OVERLAY_TEXT[name], `CommandViewController: no overlay {name}`)
	overlays[name] = provider
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

-- A room status's provider (Prompt 13: burning, blackout, rubble...): (roomId, room) -> lamp
-- sprite and a short reading, shown when the overlay tab has nothing for the room.
function CommandViewController:SetStatus(name: string, provider: Overlay?)
	statuses[name] = provider
end

-- A line added under a room's Condition in the detail panel (Prompt 13: "On fire, 64%").
function CommandViewController:SetConditionNote(fn: ((string) -> string?)?)
	conditionNote = fn
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

-- Prompt 14: notes on a rock or dug cell (dig time, progress, the queue, what a dug cell holds,
-- the Driller's hints) and the dig queue's options on rock.
function CommandViewController:SetCellNotes(fn: ((floor: number, column: number, state: string) -> { CellNote })?)
	cellNotes = fn
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

function CommandViewController:SetRockOptions(fn: ((floor: number, column: number) -> { CellOption })?)
	rockOptions = fn
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

-- Refresh the detail panel (a dig site's progress, a queue change).
function CommandViewController:Refresh()
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

-- A ghost outline for an open vote (Section 7), until HideGhost.
function CommandViewController:ShowGhost(id: string, floor: number, column: number, span: number, label: string?)
	CommandViewController:HideGhost(id)
	if not gui() then
		return
	end
	local mark = clone("CellMark")
	mark.BackgroundColor3 = CREAM
	local stroke = mark:FindFirstChildOfClass("UIStroke")
	if stroke then
		stroke.Color = CREAM
	end
	local text = mark:FindFirstChild("Label")
	if text and label then
		text.Text = string.upper(label)
		text.Visible = true
	end
	mark.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Marks")
	ghosts[id] = { Frame = mark, Floor = floor, Column = column, Span = span }
end

-- Changes a ghost's label (a site's progress: "KITCHEN 45%").
function CommandViewController:SetGhostLabel(id: string, label: string)
	local ghost = ghosts[id]
	local text = ghost and ghost.Frame:FindFirstChild("Label")
	if text then
		text.Text = string.upper(label)
		text.Visible = true
	end
end

function CommandViewController:HideGhost(id: string)
	local ghost = ghosts[id]
	if ghost then
		ghost.Frame:Destroy()
		ghosts[id] = nil
	end
end

-- Lights a room's label (by room id) rust red while on.
function CommandViewController:Blink(key: string, on: boolean)
	blinking[key] = if on then true else nil
end

function CommandViewController:State(): { [string]: any }
	local pitch = Grid.Pitch()
	return {
		Open = open,
		Center = center,
		Floors = height / pitch.Y,
		Distance = (CV.Lens(height)),
		Selected = if selected then Grid.Key(selected[1], selected[2]) else nil,
		Choice = if choice then `{choice.Action} {choice.RoomType or choice.RoomId or ""}` else nil,
		Tab = tab,
		Labels = (function()
			local n = 0
			for _ in labels do
				n += 1
			end
			return n
		end)(),
		Pings = #pings,
		Ghosts = (function()
			local n = 0
			for _ in ghosts do
				n += 1
			end
			return n
		end)(),
		Blinking = (function()
			local keys = {}
			for key in blinking do
				table.insert(keys, key)
			end
			table.sort(keys)
			return table.concat(keys, ",")
		end)(),
		FieldOfView = workspace.CurrentCamera.FieldOfView,
	}
end

-- Lifecycle ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CommandViewController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	cameraController = registry.CameraController
	ui = registry.UIController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	inRun = Constants.PlaceKind() == "Run"
	t = CV.Tuning()
end

function CommandViewController:Start()
	if not inRun then
		return
	end
	local waited = 0
	while not ui:Gui() and waited < 20 do
		waited += task.wait(0.25)
	end
	local root = ui:Gui()
	if not root or not UIContract.Find(root, "Cabinet.Pages.CommandView") then
		log:Warn("the Frame has no Command View page; it can't open")
		return
	end
	ui:Register(SCREEN, {
		Title = "Command View",
		Subtitle = "STEADFAST SHELTER CO.  ·  BUNKER IN SECTION",
		Tabs = TABS,
		Page = SCREEN,
		Docked = true,
		GamepadSelect = false,
		Hint = "Your character stays where you left it, and can be hit.",
		OnOpen = function(p: Frame)
			onOpen(p)
		end,
		OnTab = function(id: string)
			tab = id
			if open then
				refreshDetail()
			end
		end,
		OnClose = onClose,
	})
	input:On("CommandView", function()
		CommandViewController:Toggle()
	end)
	replica:Changed("Cells"):Connect(function()
		bunkerDirty = true
		if open then
			refreshDetail()
		end
	end)
	replica:Changed("Rooms"):Connect(function()
		bunkerDirty = true
		labelsDirty = true
		if open then
			refreshDetail()
		end
	end)
	-- sites, votes, unlocks and the stockpile change what the panel offers: refresh it, at most
	-- twice a second
	local pending = false
	local function soon()
		if open and not pending then
			pending = true
			task.delay(0.5, function()
				pending = false
				if open then
					refreshDetail()
				end
			end)
		end
	end
	for _, name in { "Sites", "Votes", "Unlocked", "Power", "Production", "Residents" } do
		replica:Changed(name):Connect(soon)
	end
	-- Prompt 10's Morale overlay: a room's workers' average morale
	CommandViewController:SetOverlay("Morale", function(roomId: string, _room: any): (string?, string?)
		local sum, n = 0, 0
		for _, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
			if type(resident) == "table" and resident.Job == roomId and resident.State == "Alive" then
				sum += resident.Morale or 0
				n += 1
			end
		end
		if n == 0 then
			return nil, nil
		end
		local average = math.floor(sum / n + 0.5)
		return if average >= 75 then "Lamp_Green" elseif average >= 40 then "Lamp_Amber" else "Lamp_Red", `MORALE {average}`
	end)
	-- Prompt 9's overlays: power (PowerService) and production (EconomyService)
	CommandViewController:SetOverlay("Power", function(roomId: string, room: any): (string?, string?)
		local power = replica:Get("Power", roomId)
		if type(power) ~= "table" then
			return nil, nil
		end
		if Config.Get("Rooms", room.Type).PowerOutput then
			local made = power.Made or 0
			return if made > 0 then "Lamp_Green" else "Lamp_Red", `MAKES {math.floor(made + 0.5)}`
		end
		if power.Dark then
			return "Lamp_Red", "DARK"
		end
		return "Lamp_Green", `DRAWS {power.Draw}`
	end)
	CommandViewController:SetOverlay("Production", function(roomId: string, _room: any): (string?, string?)
		local made = replica:Get("Production", roomId)
		if type(made) ~= "table" then
			return nil, nil
		end
		if made.Idle == "Dark" then
			return "Lamp_Red", "DARK"
		elseif made.Idle == "Wrecked" then
			return "Lamp_Red", "WRECKED"
		elseif made.Idle == "NoCrew" then
			return "Lamp_Amber", "NO CREW"
		end
		local resource = Config.Find("Resources", made.Makes or "")
		local what = if resource then string.upper(resource.Name) else string.upper(tostring(made.Makes))
		return "Lamp_Green", `+{made.Rate} {what}`
	end)
	for _, id in Config.Ids("Resources") do
		if RunState.Fields[id] then
			RunState.Changed(id):Connect(soon)
		end
	end
	RunState.Changed("Research"):Connect(soon)
	RunState.Changed("ReadyNeeded"):Connect(soon)
	Remotes.OnClient("CellPinged", onPinged)
	CollectionService:GetInstanceAddedSignal(FRONT_WALL_TAG):Connect(function(item: Instance)
		if open and item:IsA("BasePart") then
			Fade.Set(item, FADE_SOURCE, 1)
		end
	end)
	input.DeviceChanged:Connect(function()
		if open then
			part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Help.Text").Text = helpText()
		end
	end)
	table.insert(connections, UserInputService.InputBegan:Connect(onInputBegan))
	table.insert(connections, UserInputService.InputChanged:Connect(onInputChanged))
	table.insert(connections, UserInputService.InputEnded:Connect(onInputEnded))
	local function watchHealth(character: Model)
		local humanoid = character:WaitForChild("Humanoid", 10)
		if humanoid and humanoid:IsA("Humanoid") then
			lastHealth = humanoid.Health -- so the first hit after spawning flashes too
			humanoid.HealthChanged:Connect(function(health: number)
				if open and lastHealth and health < lastHealth then
					flashEdge()
				end
				lastHealth = health
			end)
		end
	end
	Players.LocalPlayer.CharacterAdded:Connect(watchHealth)
	if Players.LocalPlayer.Character then
		task.spawn(watchHealth, Players.LocalPlayer.Character)
	end
	RunService:BindToRenderStep(RENDER_NAME, RENDER_PRIORITY, render)
	log:Debug("Command View ready")
end

return CommandViewController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000061"><Properties><string name="Name">DevController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	DevController: the client side of DevTools.

	For players the server marked DevAllowed (everyone in Studio, admins in a live game) it
	adds a chat command: `/dev <command> [args]` (or `/d`). Commands run on the server
	(DevService checks permission again); the answer comes back as a Notice, shown in the
	chat and the output. Four commands run on the client:
	* `/dev replica <collection>` prints this client's mirror of a collection;
	* `/dev client` prints the client's replication counters;
	* `/dev clock` prints the run state as this client sees it (Run place), with the time
	  left counted on this client from the replicated server time;
	* `/dev ready [true|false]` fires the SetReady remote, as the HUD's Ready button will,
	  and reports what the server did;
	* `/dev camera` prints the over-the-shoulder camera's state; `camera.shoulder`,
	  `camera.aim [true|false]`, `camera.look <yaw> <pitch>` (degrees), `camera.zoom <studs>`
	  and `camera.cursor` (frees or locks the mouse) drive it for tests.
	* `/dev ui` prints The Frame's state; `ui.sample`, `ui.list` and `ui.dock` open the dev sample screens
	  (Lib.UISamples), `ui.open <screen>` any registered screen, `ui.close` closes, `ui.tab <id>`
	  switches tabs, `ui.main` presses the main action.
	* `/dev hud` prints the HUD's state; `hud.alert <Danger|Warning|Info> <text>`,
	  `hud.banner <text>`, `hud.slot <1-5>` and `hud.touch [true|false]` (shows the touch
	  buttons on any device, for screenshots) drive it.
	* `/dev vote` prints the vote telegram (what it shows, your vote) and the Command View's
	  ghosts; the server's `votes`, `vote.yes|no [n]`, `vote.end` and `vote.bots` run votes.
	* `/dev cv` prints the Command View's state (with the detail panel's options); `cv.open`,
	  `cv.close`, `cv.select <floor> <column>` and `cv.ping` drive it; `cv.ghost <floor> <column>
	  <span> [label]` / `cv.unghost` show a vote's ghost outline, `cv.blink <roomId> [false]` blinks
	  a room's label, `cv.overlay <Power|Morale|Threat|Production> [false]` sets a sample reading.

	In Studio it also makes PlayerScripts.DevInvoke (a BindableFunction) so tools can run the
	same commands from the Client datamodel: DevInvoke:Invoke("replica _SelfTest").
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TextChatService = game:GetService("TextChatService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local UISamples = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("UISamples"))
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local TableUtil = require(Shared.Utilities.TableUtil)

local log = Log.new("DevController")
local CHAT_LINES = 12

local DevController = {
	Name = "DevController",
	Dependencies = {
		"ReplicaController",
		"InputController",
		"CameraController",
		"UIController",
		"HUDController",
		"CommandViewController",
		"VoteController",
	},
}

local replica: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local ui: any = nil
local hud: any = nil
local registryInput: any = nil
local commandView: any = nil
local voteView: any = nil
local devCursorFree = false
local lastNotice: string? = nil
local commandMade = false

local function dump(value: any, depth: number?): string
	local level = depth or 0
	if type(value) == "string" then
		return if value == "\0none" then "NONE" else string.format("%q", value)
	elseif typeof(value) == "Vector3" then
		return string.format("(%g, %g, %g)", value.X, value.Y, value.Z)
	elseif type(value) ~= "table" then
		return tostring(value)
	elseif level > 4 then
		return "{...}"
	end
	local parts = {}
	for _, key in TableUtil.SortedKeys(value) do
		table.insert(parts, `{tostring(key)}={dump(value[key], level + 1)}`)
	end
	return "{" .. table.concat(parts, ", ") .. "}"
end

local function escape(text: string): string
	return (string.gsub(string.gsub(string.gsub(text, "&", "&amp;"), "<", "&lt;"), ">", "&gt;"))
end

local function show(text: string)
	print(`[100Y dev] {text}`)
	local channels = TextChatService:FindFirstChild("TextChannels")
	local system = channels and channels:FindFirstChild("RBXSystem")
	if system and system:IsA("TextChannel") then
		local lines = string.split(text, "\n")
		for index = 1, math.min(#lines, CHAT_LINES) do
			pcall(system.DisplaySystemMessage, system, escape(lines[index]))
		end
		if #lines > CHAT_LINES then
			pcall(system.DisplaySystemMessage, system, `... {#lines - CHAT_LINES} more lines in the output (F9)`)
		end
	end
end

local function parse(text: string): (string, { any })
	local words = {}
	for word in string.gmatch(text, "%S+") do
		local number = tonumber(word)
		if word == "true" or word == "false" then
			table.insert(words, word == "true")
		elseif number ~= nil and number == number and math.abs(number) ~= math.huge then
			table.insert(words, number)
		else
			table.insert(words, string.sub(word, 1, 120))
		end
	end
	local name = table.remove(words, 1)
	return if type(name) == "string" then name else "help", words
end

local function describeClock(): string
	local runPhase = RunState.Get("RunPhase")
	if runPhase == nil then
		return "no run state in this place"
	end
	local left = RunState.TimeLeft()
	local leftText = if RunState.Get("PhaseOpen") then "no timer (until its boss is beaten)"
		elseif left then string.format("%.1f s left", left)
		else "stopped"
	local boss = RunState.Get("SurgeBoss")
	local bossText = if boss then ` ({boss})` else ""
	return `client sees: {runPhase}, cycle {RunState.Get("Cycle")}, Year {RunState.Get("Year")} ({RunState.Get("Era")}), `
		.. `{RunState.Get("CyclePhase") or "-"} {leftText}, siren {tostring(RunState.Get("Siren") == true)}, `
		.. `Surge {RunState.Get("SurgeKind") or "-"}{bossText}, {RunState.Get("YearsPerCycle")} years per cycle, `
		.. `ready {RunState.Get("ReadyCount") or 0}/{RunState.Get("ReadyNeeded") or 0}`
end

local function pressReady(on: boolean): string
	if not Remotes.InPlace("SetReady") then
		return "there is no run clock in this place"
	end
	local player = Players.LocalPlayer
	Remotes.FireServer("SetReady", on)
	local waited = 0
	while waited < 2 and player:GetAttribute("Ready") ~= on and not (on and RunState.Get("Siren") == true) do
		waited += task.wait()
	end
	return `SetReady {on}: my Ready is {tostring(player:GetAttribute("Ready"))}\n{describeClock()}`
end

local function describeUI(): string
	task.wait()
	local gui = ui:Gui()
	if not gui then
		return "ui: no Frame in this place"
	end
	local page = ui:Page()
	local items = 0
	if page then
		local content = page:FindFirstChild("Content")
		for _, name in { "Grid", "List" } do
			local holder = content and content:FindFirstChild(name)
			if holder and holder:IsA("GuiObject") and holder.Visible then
				for _, child in holder:GetChildren() do
					if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
						items += 1
					end
				end
			end
		end
	end
	return string.format(
		"ui: %s, screen %s, tab %s, %d items, cursor free %s, input blocked %s",
		if gui.Enabled then "open" else "closed",
		tostring(ui:Current()),
		tostring(ui:CurrentTab()),
		items,
		tostring(camera:State().CursorFree),
		tostring(registryInput:IsBlocked())
	)
end

local function describeHUD(): string
	task.wait()
	local state = hud:State()
	if not state.Present then
		return "hud: no HUD in this place"
	end
	return string.format(
		"hud: %s, year %s, phase %s, time %s, ready button %s, slot %d, touch %s, class %s",
		if state.Enabled then "shown" elseif state.Hidden then "hidden (a menu is open)" else "hidden",
		tostring(state.Year),
		tostring(state.Phase),
		tostring(state.TimeLeft),
		tostring(state.Ready),
		state.Slot,
		tostring(state.Touch),
		tostring(state.Class)
	)
end

local function describeCommandView(): string
	task.wait()
	task.wait()
	local state = commandView:State()
	local main = ""
	local gui = ui:Gui()
	local button = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Cabinet") and gui.Cabinet:FindFirstChild("MainAction")
	if button and button.Visible then
		main = `, main action "{button.Content.Label.Text}" ({if button:GetAttribute("Disabled") then "greyed out" else "live"})`
	end
	local detail = ""
	local page = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Cabinet") and gui.Cabinet.Pages:FindFirstChild("CommandView")
	if page then
		local options = {}
		for _, row in page.Detail.Options:GetChildren() do
			if row:IsA("GuiObject") then
				table.insert(options, { row.LayoutOrder, `{row:FindFirstChild("Name").Text} ({row:FindFirstChild("Value").Text})` })
			end
		end
		table.sort(options, function(a, b)
			return a[1] < b[1]
		end)
		local names = {}
		for i, option in options do
			if i <= 24 then
				table.insert(names, `{i}. {option[2]}`)
			end
		end
		detail = `\n  detail: {page.Detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text} / {page.Detail.Sub.Text}`
			.. (if #names > 0 then "\n  options: " .. table.concat(names, "; ") else "")
	end
	return string.format(
		"command view: %s, centre (%.0f, %.0f), %.1f floors high, camera %.0f studs away, FOV %.1f, selected %s, choice %s, tab %s, %d labels, %d pings",
		if state.Open then "open" else "closed",
		state.Center.X,
		state.Center.Y,
		state.Floors,
		state.Distance,
		state.FieldOfView,
		tostring(state.Selected),
		tostring(state.Choice),
		state.Tab,
		state.Labels,
		state.Pings
	) .. (if state.Ghosts > 0 then `, {state.Ghosts} ghost(s)` else "")
		.. (if state.Blinking ~= "" then `, blinking {state.Blinking}` else "") .. main .. detail
end

local function describeCamera(): string
	task.wait() -- let a frame apply what the command changed
	task.wait()
	local state = camera:State()
	local p = state.Position
	return string.format(
		"camera: %s, %s shoulder, yaw %.0f, pitch %.0f, zoom %.1f (wanted %.1f), %s%s, FOV %.0f, %s%s, %d faded, device %s%s at (%.1f, %.1f, %.1f)",
		if state.Stopped then "STOPPED (Roblox camera)" elseif state.Active then "on" else "suspended",
		state.Shoulder,
		state.Yaw,
		state.Pitch,
		state.Distance,
		state.Wanted,
		if state.Indoors then "indoors" else "outdoors",
		if state.Blocked then ", held in by a wall" else "",
		state.FieldOfView,
		if state.Aiming then "aiming" else "not aiming",
		if state.CursorFree then ", cursor free" else "",
		state.Fading,
		state.Device,
		if state.Suspended then ", suspended" else "",
		p.X,
		p.Y,
		p.Z
	)
end

-- Runs a command line; client-side commands answer here, the rest go to the server.
local function run(text: string): string?
	local name, args = parse(text)
	if name == "replica" then
		local collection = tostring(args[1] or "")
		local values = replica:All(collection)
		local keys = TableUtil.SortedKeys(values)
		if #keys == 0 then
			return `{collection}: empty on this client`
		end
		local lines = { `{collection}: {#keys} values` }
		for _, key in keys do
			table.insert(lines, `  {key} = {dump(values[key])}`)
		end
		return table.concat(lines, "\n")
	elseif name == "client" then
		local stats = replica:Stats()
		return `client: ready={tostring(replica:IsReady())}, delta events {stats.Events}, ops {stats.Ops}, snapshots {stats.Snapshots}`
	elseif name == "clock" then
		return describeClock()
	elseif name == "ready" then
		return pressReady(args[1] ~= false)
	elseif name == "camera" then
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.shoulder" then
		camera:SwapShoulder()
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.aim" then
		camera:SetAiming(args[1] ~= false)
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.look" then
		camera:SetLook(tonumber(args[1]) or 0, tonumber(args[2]) or 0)
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.zoom" then
		camera:SetZoom(tonumber(args[1]) or 9)
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.cursor" then
		devCursorFree = not devCursorFree
		camera:FreeCursor("DevTools", devCursorFree)
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "ui" then
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.sample" or name == "ui.list" or name == "ui.dock" then
		UISamples.Register(ui, replica)
		ui:Open(if name == "ui.sample" then "Sample" elseif name == "ui.list" then "SampleList" else "SampleDocked")
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.open" then
		UISamples.Register(ui, replica)
		ui:Open(tostring(args[1] or "Sample"))
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.close" then
		ui:Close()
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.tab" then
		ui:SelectTab(tostring(args[1] or ""))
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.main" then
		ui:PressMainAction()
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "hud" then
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "hud.alert" then
		local kind = tostring(args[1] or "Warning")
		local words = {}
		for i = 2, #args do
			table.insert(words, tostring(args[i]))
		end
		hud:Alert(if kind == "Danger" or kind == "Info" then kind else "Warning", table.concat(words, " "))
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "hud.banner" then
		local words = {}
		for _, word in args do
			table.insert(words, tostring(word))
		end
		hud:Banner(table.concat(words, " "), "Warning", 6)
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "hud.slot" then
		hud:SelectSlot(tonumber(args[1]) or 1)
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "hud.touch" then
		hud:SetForceTouch(args[1] ~= false)
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "vote" then
		local state = voteView:State()
		return `vote telegram: {if state.Visible then "showing " .. tostring(state.Shown) else "hidden"}`
			.. (if state.Visible then `\n  {state.Proposal}\n  {state.Tally}\n  your vote: {tostring(state.Mine)}` else "")
			.. `\n  ghosts: {if state.Ghosts ~= "" then state.Ghosts else "none"}`
	elseif name == "cv" then
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.open" or name == "cv.close" then
		if commandView:IsOpen() ~= (name == "cv.open") then
			commandView:Toggle()
		end
		task.wait(0.5)
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.select" then
		commandView:Select(tonumber(args[1]), tonumber(args[2]))
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.ping" then
		local state = commandView:State()
		if not state.Selected then
			return "cv.ping: select a cell first (cv.select <floor> <column>)"
		end
		local floor, column = string.match(state.Selected, "^(%-?%d+),(%-?%d+)$")
		Remotes.FireServer("PingCell", tonumber(floor), tonumber(column))
		task.wait(0.5)
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.ghost" then
		-- the outline a vote will show for a proposed room (Prompt 8 calls ShowGhost)
		commandView:ShowGhost("dev", tonumber(args[1]) or 2, tonumber(args[2]) or 3, tonumber(args[3]) or 1,
			if args[4] ~= nil then tostring(args[4]) else "Proposed")
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.unghost" then
		commandView:HideGhost("dev")
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.blink" then
		commandView:Blink(tostring(args[1] or "R1"), args[2] ~= false)
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.overlay" then
		-- a sample reading for screenshots (green, amber, red by room number), until the systems
		-- that own each overlay register real ones
		local overlay = tostring(args[1] or "Power")
		if args[2] == false then
			commandView:SetOverlay(overlay, nil)
		else
			local lamps = { "Lamp_Green", "Lamp_Amber", "Lamp_Red" }
			commandView:SetOverlay(overlay, function(roomId: string): string?
				return lamps[(tonumber(string.match(roomId, "%d+")) or 0) % 3 + 1]
			end)
		end
		return describeCommandView()
	end
	if #args > 8 then
		return "at most 8 arguments"
	end
	Remotes.FireServer("DevCommand", string.sub(name, 1, 48), args)
	return nil
end

local function makeChatCommand()
	if commandMade or Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("DevAllowed") ~= true then
		return
	end
	commandMade = true
	local command = Instance.new("TextChatCommand")
	command.Name = "DevCommand"
	command.PrimaryAlias = "/dev"
	command.SecondaryAlias = "/d"
	command.Triggered:Connect(function(_source: TextSource, message: string)
		local rest = string.match(message, "^%S+%s*(.*)$") or ""
		local answer = run(if rest == "" then "help" else rest)
		if answer then
			show(answer)
		end
	end)
	command.Parent = TextChatService
	log:Debug("/dev ready")
end

function DevController:Init(registry)
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	camera = registry.CameraController
	ui = registry.UIController
	hud = registry.HUDController
	registryInput = registry.InputController
	commandView = registry.CommandViewController
	voteView = registry.VoteController
	Remotes.OnClient("Notice", function(text: any)
		if type(text) == "string" then
			lastNotice = text
			show(text)
		end
	end)
end

function DevController:Start()
	local player = Players.LocalPlayer
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("DevAllowed"):Connect(makeChatCommand)
	makeChatCommand()

	if RunService:IsStudio() then
		local invoke = Instance.new("BindableFunction")
		invoke.Name = "DevInvoke"
		invoke.OnInvoke = function(line: any): string
			if type(line) ~= "string" then
				return "usage: DevInvoke:Invoke(\"replica Rooms\")"
			end
			lastNotice = nil
			local answer = run(line)
			if answer then
				return answer
			end
			local waited = 0
			while lastNotice == nil and waited < 5 do
				waited += task.wait()
			end
			return lastNotice or "no answer from the server within 5 s"
		end
		invoke.Parent = script.Parent.Parent
	end
end

return DevController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000062"><Properties><string name="Name">HUDController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	HUDController: the run HUD (bible Section 18), StarterGui.HUD in the Run place. Fixed
	positions, separate from The Frame; this controller only fills the layout in.

	Live now:
	* Top centre: the year flip counter (the tiles flip when the year changes), the era, the
	  cycle dial (day, then Surge) with the phase and the time left, and the Ready button with
	  the team's count (the SetReady remote). A boss Surge has no timer.
	* Banners under the vote telegram: the siren and the start of each Surge.
	* Top left: health from the character; the class and its ability (the Survivor until the
	  loadout arrives); stamina and radiation rest until combat.
	* Top right: the stockpile chips (values come with the economy, Prompt 9), the seismograph
	  (Disturbance, Prompt 14: the trace swings wider as it rises, a Tremor throws it wide, and the
	  reading says CALM, RISING, UNSETTLED or DANGER) and the Command View button.
	* Bottom centre: the hotbar's selection (1 to 5, the D-pad, a tap).
	* Bottom right on touch: Fire, Aim, Melee, Ability, Interact, Jump, Dodge, Sprint (a
	  toggle), Ping and Shoulder, bound through InputController. Roblox's own jump button is
	  hidden while ours shows.

	On PC the camera locks the mouse; a click of the mouse wheel frees the cursor to click HUD
	buttons, and another click locks it again. Ready has its own key (Z, D-pad down).

	For later systems: Alert(kind, text) for the alert feed, Banner(text, kind) for
	announcements, HoldBanner(reason, on) while something else owns the banner's place (Prompt
	13: the meltdown telegram), SetVital, SetClass, SetResource, SetSlot and the HotbarSelected
	signal.

	The HUD hides during the intro and while a Frame screen is open.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local StarterGui = game:GetService("StarterGui")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Dig = require(Shared.Rules.Dig)
local Hud = require(Shared.Rules.Hud)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local UIContract = require(Shared.UIContract)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))
local UIKit = require(Lib:WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local log = Log.new("HUDController")

export type AlertKind = "Danger" | "Warning" | "Info"

local COLORS = {
	cream = Color3.fromHex("#F2E6C9"),
	navy = Color3.fromHex("#1B2A3A"),
	hazard = Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E"),
	signal = Color3.fromHex("#E8743B"),
	leaf = Color3.fromHex("#7CC26A"),
	rust = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B"),
}
-- The stockpile chips: Section 18 lists power, Food, Water, Scrap, ore and Ammo.
local STOCK = {
	{ Id = "Power", Icon = "Icon_Power" },
	{ Id = "Food", Icon = "Icon_Food" },
	{ Id = "Water", Icon = "Icon_Water" },
	{ Id = "Scrap", Icon = "Icon_Scrap" },
	{ Id = "Iron", Icon = "Icon_Iron" },
	{ Id = "Copper", Icon = "Icon_Copper" },
	{ Id = "Crystal", Icon = "Icon_Crystal" },
	{ Id = "Ammo", Icon = "Icon_Ammo" },
}
-- Touch buttons and the actions they drive (Jump and the Sprint toggle are handled here).
local TOUCH_ACTIONS = {
	Fire = "Fire",
	Aim = "Aim",
	Melee = "Melee",
	Ability = "Ability",
	Interact = "Interact",
	Dodge = "Dodge",
	Ping = "Ping",
	Shoulder = "SwapShoulder",
	Heal = "Heal", -- Landon, 2026-11-08
}
local ABILITY_ICONS: { [string]: string } = { Security = "Icon_Shield" } -- more with the class icons (A11)
local MAX_ALERTS = 3
local FLIP_SECONDS = 0.07
local TICK_SECONDS = 0.1

local HUDController = {
	Name = "HUDController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "UIController", "CameraController", "ReplicaController" },
	HotbarSelected = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<number>,
}

local input: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local ui: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local gui: ScreenGui? = nil
local inRun = false
local hidden: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local forceTouch = false
local sprintOn = false
local selectedSlot = 1
local alertCount = 0
local bannerToken = 0
local shownYear: number? = nil
local digitHome: { [Instance]: { UDim2 } } = {}
local resourceChips: { [string]: any } = {}
local jumpGuard: RBXScriptConnection? = nil
local classId = "Survivor"
local classLevel = 1

local function part(path: string): any
	assert(gui, "HUDController: no HUD")
	local found = UIContract.Find(gui, path)
	assert(found, `HUDController: HUD.{path} is missing (see Shared.UIContract)`)
	return found
end

local function clone(template: string): any
	local copy = part("Templates." .. template):Clone()
	copy.Visible = true
	return copy
end

local function humanoid(): Humanoid?
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	return if character then character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid") else nil
end

local function refreshVisible()
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local phase = RunState.Get("RunPhase")
	local live = inRun and (phase == "Playing" or phase == "Ended")
	gui.Enabled = live and next(hidden) == nil
end

-- Top centre --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function flip(digit: TextLabel, value: string)
	local home = digitHome[digit]
	if not home then
		home = { digit.Size, digit.Position }
		digitHome[digit] = home
	end
	if digit.Text == value then
		return
	end
	local size, position = home[1], home[2]
	local squash = TweenService:Create(digit, TweenInfo.new(FLIP_SECONDS, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.In), {
		Size = UDim2.new(size.X.Scale, 0, 0, 0),
		Position = UDim2.new(position.X.Scale, 0, position.Y.Scale + size.Y.Scale / 2, 0),
	})
	squash.Completed:Once(function()
		digit.Text = value
		TweenService:Create(digit, TweenInfo.new(FLIP_SECONDS, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.Out), {
			Size = size,
			Position = position,
		}):Play()
	end)
	squash:Play()
end

local function showYear()
	local year = RunState.Get("Year")
	if type(year) ~= "number" then
		return
	end
	local digits = Hud.YearDigits(year)
	for i = 1, 3 do
		local digit = part(`YearClock.Tile{i}.Digit`)
		if shownYear == nil then
			digit.Text = digits[i]
		else
			flip(digit, digits[i])
		end
	end
	shownYear = year
end

local function showEra()
	local id = RunState.Get("Era")
	local era = if type(id) == "string" then Config.Find("Eras", id) else nil
	if not era then
		part("YearClock.Era").Text = ""
		part("YearClock.EraName").Text = ""
		return
	end
	local index = table.find(Config.Ids("Eras"), id)
	part("YearClock.Era").Text = "ERA " .. Hud.Numeral(index or 1)
	part("YearClock.EraName").Text = string.upper(era.Name)
end

local function bossName(): string
	local id = RunState.Get("SurgeBoss")
	local boss = if type(id) == "string" then Config.Find("Bosses", id) else nil
	return if boss then string.upper(boss.Name) else "THE BOSS"
end

local function tickClock()
	local phase = RunState.Get("CyclePhase")
	local open = RunState.Get("PhaseOpen") == true
	local siren = RunState.Get("Siren") == true
	local left = RunState.TimeLeft()
	local scale = RunState.Get("TimeScale")
	local length = RunState.Get("PhaseLength")
	local realLength = if type(length) == "number" then length / (if type(scale) == "number" and scale > 0 then scale else 1) else nil
	local clock = Config.Get("Tuning", "Clock")
	local pointer = part("CycleDial.Pointer")
	pointer.Position = UDim2.fromScale(
		Hud.DialPosition(phase, realLength, left, open, clock.DaySeconds, clock.SurgeSeconds),
		pointer.Position.Y.Scale
	)
	local phaseText, phaseColor = "", COLORS.cream
	if phase == "Day" then
		phaseText = if siren then "SIREN" else `DAY {RunState.Get("Cycle") or 1}`
		phaseColor = if siren then COLORS.hazard else COLORS.cream
	elseif phase == "Surge" then
		local kind = RunState.Get("SurgeKind")
		phaseText = if kind == "Boss" or kind == "Final" then "BOSS" else "SURGE"
		phaseColor = COLORS.signal
	end
	local phaseLabel = part("Phase.Text")
	phaseLabel.Text = phaseText
	phaseLabel.TextColor3 = phaseColor
	local timeLabel = part("TimeLeft.Text")
	timeLabel.Text = if open then "--:--" else Hud.Clock(left)
	timeLabel.TextColor3 = if siren and (os.clock() % 1) < 0.5 then COLORS.hazard else COLORS.cream

	local ready = part("Ready")
	local canReady = RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Playing" and phase == "Day" and not siren
		and (RunState.Get("ReadyNeeded") or 0) > 0
	ready.Visible = canReady
	if canReady then
		local mine = Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("Ready") == true
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(part("Ready.Content.Lamp"), if mine then "Lamp_Green" else "Lamp_Off")
		part("Ready.Content.Count").Text = `{RunState.Get("ReadyCount") or 0} OF {RunState.Get("ReadyNeeded") or 0}`
	end
end

-- Banners and alerts ----------------------------------------------------------------------

local function bannerStyle(kind: AlertKind): (string, Color3)
	if kind == "Danger" then
		return "Alert_Danger", COLORS.signal
	elseif kind == "Info" then
		return "Alert_Info", COLORS.cream
	end
	return "Alert_Warning", COLORS.hazard
end

local bannerHolds: { [string]: boolean } = {}

-- Keeps the banner hidden while `reason` holds its place (the meltdown telegram, Prompt 13).
function HUDController:HoldBanner(reason: string, on: boolean)
	bannerHolds[reason] = if on then true else nil
	if on and gui then
		part("Banner").Visible = false
	end
end

function HUDController:Banner(text: string, kind: AlertKind?, seconds: number?)
	if not gui or next(bannerHolds) then
		return
	end
	local sprite, color = bannerStyle(kind or "Warning")
	local banner = part("Banner")
	KitRuntime.SetSprite(part("Banner.Icon"), sprite)
	local label = part("Banner.Text")
	label.Text = string.upper(text)
	label.TextColor3 = color
	banner.Visible = true
	bannerToken += 1
	local token = bannerToken
	task.delay(seconds or 4, function()
		if token == bannerToken then
			banner.Visible = false
		end
	end)
end

function HUDController:Alert(kind: AlertKind, text: string, seconds: number?)
	if hidden.Frame and ui then
		ui:Notice(text, kind) -- a screen hides the HUD: say it in the screen's footer instead
	end
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local holder = part("Alerts")
	local slips = {}
	for _, child in holder:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			table.insert(slips, child)
		end
	end
	table.sort(slips, function(a, b)
		return a.LayoutOrder > b.LayoutOrder -- oldest last
	end)
	while #slips >= MAX_ALERTS do
		local oldest = table.remove(slips) :: GuiObject
		oldest:Destroy()
	end
	alertCount += 1
	local slip = clone("AlertSlip")
	slip.Name = "Alert" .. alertCount
	slip.LayoutOrder = -alertCount -- newest on top
	KitRuntime.SetSprite(slip.Icon, (bannerStyle(kind)))
	slip.Text.Text = string.upper(text)
	slip.Parent = holder
	task.delay(seconds or 8, function()
		if slip.Parent then
			slip:Destroy()
		end
	end)
end

local function onSiren()
	if RunState.Get("Siren") ~= true then
		return
	end
	local kind = RunState.Get("SurgeKind")
	local who = if kind == "Boss" or kind == "Final" then bossName() else "SURGE"
	HUDController:Banner(`SIREN  ·  {who} IN 0:20`, "Warning", 5)
end

local function onPhase()
	if RunState.Get("CyclePhase") ~= "Surge" then
		return
	end
	if RunState.Get("PhaseOpen") == true then
		HUDController:Banner(`{bossName()}  ·  THE SURGE ENDS WHEN IT FALLS`, "Danger", 6)
	else
		HUDController:Banner("SURGE  ·  HOLD THE BUNKER", "Danger", 4)
	end
end

-- Top left --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HUDController:SetVital(name: string, fraction: number, text: string?)
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	part(`Vitals.{name}.Needle`).Rotation = Hud.NeedleRotation(fraction)
	if text then
		local value: any = UIContract.Find(gui, `Vitals.{name}.Value`)
		if value then
			value.Text = text
		end
	end
end

local function watchHealth(character: Model)
	local h = character:WaitForChild("Humanoid", 10)
	if not h or not h:IsA("Humanoid") then
		return
	end
	local function update()
		local max = math.max(h.MaxHealth, 1)
		HUDController:SetVital("Health", h.Health / max, tostring(math.max(0, math.ceil(h.Health))))
	end
	h.HealthChanged:Connect(update)
	h:GetPropertyChangedSignal("MaxHealth"):Connect(update)
	update()
end

local function keyText(): string
	local device = input:Device()
	return if device == "Gamepad" then "LB" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "Q" else ""
end

-- Ready's own key (Landon, 2026-11-08): Z on PC, the D-pad's down on console (InputController).
local function readyKeyText(): string
	local device = input:Device()
	return if device == "Gamepad" then "DOWN" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "Z" else ""
end

function HUDController:SetClass(id: string, level: number?)
	local class = Config.Find("Classes", id)
	if not class or not gui then
		return
	end
	classId = id
	classLevel = level or 1
	part("Vitals.AbilityName").Text = string.upper(class.Ability.Name)
	part("Vitals.Class").Text = `{string.upper(class.Name)}  ·  LV {classLevel}`
	local icon = part("Vitals.Ability.Icon")
	local sprite = ABILITY_ICONS[id]
	icon.Visible = sprite ~= nil
	if sprite then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(icon, sprite)
	end
	local touchIcon = part("Touch.Ability.Content.Icon")
	if sprite then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(touchIcon, sprite)
	end
end

-- Top right -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HUDController:SetResource(id: string, text: string, lamp: string?)
	local chip = resourceChips[id]
	if not chip then
		return
	end
	chip.Value.Text = text
	chip.Lamp.Visible = lamp ~= nil
	if lamp then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(chip.Lamp, lamp)
	end
end

local cursorFree = false -- PC: the mouse wheel freed the cursor for the HUD

-- Copper and Crystal chips stay hidden until the team digs into their bands (Config.DepthBands).
local function refreshOreChips()
	local deepest = 1 -- the run starts with floors 1 and 2 built
	for key in replica:All("Cells") do
		local floor = Grid.Parse(key)
		if floor and floor > deepest then
			deepest = floor
		end
	end
	for _, band in Config.All("DepthBands") do
		local chip = if band.Ore then resourceChips[band.Ore] else nil
		if chip then
			chip.Visible = deepest >= band.Floors.From
		end
	end
end

local function buildStockpile()
	local holder = part("Stockpile.Resources")
	for _, child in holder:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			child:Destroy()
		end
	end
	for i, entry in STOCK do
		if Config.Find("Resources", entry.Id) and UIKit.Sprites[entry.Icon] then
			local chip = clone("ResourceChip")
			chip.Name = entry.Id
			chip.LayoutOrder = i
			KitRuntime.SetSprite(chip.Icon, entry.Icon)
			chip.Value.Text = "—"
			chip.Parent = holder
			resourceChips[entry.Id] = chip
		end
	end
	HUDController:SetResource("Power", "—", "Lamp_Off")
end

-- Hotbar ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HUDController:SelectSlot(index: number)
	if not gui or index < 1 or index > 5 then
		return
	end
	selectedSlot = index
	for i = 1, 5 do
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(part(`Hotbar.Slot{i}`), if i == index then "Hotbar_Selected" else "Hotbar_Slot")
	end
	HUDController.HotbarSelected:Fire(index)
end

function HUDController:SelectedSlot(): number
	return selectedSlot
end

-- A hotbar slot's item icon (a kit sprite) and ammo text; nil empties it.
function HUDController:SetSlot(index: number, icon: string?, ammo: string?)
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local item = part(`Hotbar.Slot{index}.Item`)
	item.Visible = icon ~= nil
	if icon then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(item, icon)
	end
	local count = part(`Hotbar.Slot{index}.Ammo`)
	count.Visible = ammo ~= nil
	count.Text = ammo or ""
end

-- Touch -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function robloxJumpButton(): GuiObject?
	local touchGui = Players.LocalPlayer:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
	touchGui = touchGui and touchGui:FindFirstChild("TouchGui")
	local frame = touchGui and touchGui:FindFirstChild("TouchControlFrame")
	local jump = frame and frame:FindFirstChild("JumpButton")
	return if jump and jump:IsA("GuiObject") then jump else nil
end

local function guardRobloxJump(on: boolean)
	if jumpGuard then
		jumpGuard:Disconnect()
		jumpGuard = nil
	end
	local jump = robloxJumpButton()
	if not jump then
		return
	end
	if on then
		jump.Visible = false
		jumpGuard = jump:GetPropertyChangedSignal("Visible"):Connect(function()
			if jump.Visible then
				jump.Visible = false
			end
		end)
	end
end

local function refreshDevice()
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local device = input:Device()
	local touch = forceTouch or device == "Touch"
	part("Touch").Visible = touch
	guardRobloxJump(touch and device == "Touch")
	local key = keyText()
	part("Vitals.Ability.Key").Visible = key ~= ""
	part("Vitals.Ability.Key.Text").Text = key
	local readyKey = readyKeyText()
	part("Ready.Key").Visible = readyKey ~= ""
	part("Ready.Key.Text").Text = readyKey
	local viewKey = part("CommandView.Content.Key")
	viewKey.Text = if device == "Gamepad" then "VIEW" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "TAB" else ""
	for i = 1, 5 do
		part(`Hotbar.Slot{i}.Key`).Visible = device == "Keyboard"
	end
	-- the Heal key on the Medkits chip (Landon, 2026-11-08): H, or a hold of D-pad up
	local healKey = if device == "Gamepad" then "UP" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "H" else ""
	part("Medkits.Key").Visible = healKey ~= ""
	part("Medkits.Key.Text").Text = healKey
end

local function setSprintToggle(on: boolean)
	sprintOn = on
	input:Press("Sprint", on, "TouchToggle")
	local button = part("Touch.Sprint")
	local up, down = button:GetAttribute("RectUp"), button:GetAttribute("RectDown")
	if on and not button:GetAttribute("RestUp") then
		button:SetAttribute("RestUp", up)
		button:SetAttribute("RectUp", down) -- stays pressed while on
	elseif not on and button:GetAttribute("RestUp") then
		button:SetAttribute("RectUp", button:GetAttribute("RestUp"))
		button:SetAttribute("RestUp", nil)
	end
	button.ImageRectOffset = button:GetAttribute("RectUp")
end

local function bindTouch()
	for name, action in TOUCH_ACTIONS do
		input:BindButton(action, part("Touch." .. name))
	end
	part("Touch.Sprint").Activated:Connect(function()
		setSprintToggle(not sprintOn)
	end)
	local jump = part("Touch.Jump")
	jump.MouseButton1Down:Connect(function()
		local h = humanoid()
		if h then
			h.Jump = true
		end
	end)
end

-- Lifecycle -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HUDController:SetForceTouch(on: boolean)
	forceTouch = on
	refreshDevice()
end

function HUDController:Hide(reason: string, on: boolean)
	hidden[reason] = if on then true else nil
	refreshVisible()
end

function HUDController:State(): { [string]: any }
	return {
		Present = gui ~= nil,
		Enabled = gui ~= nil and gui.Enabled,
		Year = shownYear,
		Phase = if gui then part("Phase.Text").Text else nil,
		TimeLeft = if gui then part("TimeLeft.Text").Text else nil,
		Ready = if gui then part("Ready").Visible else nil,
		Slot = selectedSlot,
		Touch = if gui then part("Touch").Visible else nil,
		Class = classId,
		Hidden = next(hidden) ~= nil,
	}
end

function HUDController:Gui(): ScreenGui?
	return gui
end

function HUDController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	ui = registry.UIController
	camera = registry.CameraController
	inRun = Constants.PlaceKind() == "Run"
end

-- The seismograph (Section 10: Disturbance shown as a seismograph on the HUD; Prompt 14) ----------
-- The trace scrolls across the paper; its swing grows with Disturbance, a Tremor throws it wide
-- for a moment, and the reading under DISTURBANCE says how close the next breach or Tremor is.

local SEISMO_HZ = 20
local seismoValue = 0
local seismoTremorUntil = 0
local seismoPhase = 0
local LEVEL_COLORS = { CALM = "leaf", RISING = "hazard", UNSETTLED = "signal", DANGER = "rust" }

local function showDisturbance()
	local value = RunState.Get("Disturbance")
	seismoValue = if type(value) == "number" then value else 0
	local level = Dig.Level(seismoValue)
	local label = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("DisturbanceLevel")
	if label and label:IsA("TextLabel") then
		label.Text = level
		label.TextColor3 = COLORS[LEVEL_COLORS[level] or "leaf"]
	end
end

local function tickSeismograph(dt: number)
	local seis = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Disturbance")
	local trace = seis and seis:FindFirstChild("Trace")
	if not trace then
		return
	end
	seismoPhase += dt
	local max = Dig.DisturbanceTuning().Max
	local swing = 0.03 + 0.34 * math.clamp(seismoValue / max, 0, 1)
	if os.clock() < seismoTremorUntil then
		swing = 0.45
	end
	for _, segment in trace:GetChildren() do
		if segment:IsA("GuiObject") then
			local i = tonumber(string.sub(segment.Name, 2)) or 0
			-- newer readings on the right; the paper runs left
			local y = math.noise(i * 0.35 - seismoPhase * 6, seismoPhase * 0.7) * swing * 2
			segment.Position = UDim2.fromScale(segment.Position.X.Scale, 0.5 + math.clamp(y, -0.46, 0.46))
		end
	end
	local label = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("DisturbanceLevel")
	if label and label:IsA("TextLabel") then
		-- DANGER blinks: the next step is a Tremor
		label.TextTransparency = if Dig.Level(seismoValue) == "DANGER" and os.clock() % 0.8 < 0.3 then 0.6 else 0
	end
end

function HUDController:Start()
	if not inRun then
		return -- the Lobby's own HUD comes with the lobby (Prompt 21)
	end
	local playerGui = Players.LocalPlayer:WaitForChild("PlayerGui")
	local found = playerGui:WaitForChild("HUD", 20)
	if not found or not found:IsA("ScreenGui") then
		log:Warn("no HUD ScreenGui in this place")
		return
	end
	gui = found
	KitRuntime.Watch(found)
	-- Tab opens the Command View (bible Section 7), so Roblox's player list (also on Tab) is off
	-- in the run.
	pcall(function()
		StarterGui:SetCoreGuiEnabled(Enum.CoreGuiType.PlayerList, false)
	end)
	buildStockpile()
	HUDController:SetClass("Survivor", 1)
	HUDController:SetVital("Stamina", 1)
	HUDController:SetVital("Radiation", 0)
	HUDController:SelectSlot(1)
	bindTouch()
	refreshDevice()
	input.DeviceChanged:Connect(refreshDevice)

	-- power (PowerService): what every room would draw against what is made; the lamp is red
	-- while rooms are dark, amber past PowerWarnAt of the power made, green otherwise
	local function showPower()
		local made, needed = RunState.Get("PowerMade"), RunState.Get("PowerNeeded")
		if type(made) ~= "number" or type(needed) ~= "number" then
			HUDController:SetResource("Power", "—", "Lamp_Off")
			return
		end
		local darkRooms = RunState.Get("DarkRooms")
		local lamp = if type(darkRooms) == "number" and darkRooms > 0 then "Lamp_Red"
			elseif needed > made * Config.Get("Tuning", "Rooms").PowerWarnAt then "Lamp_Amber"
			else "Lamp_Green"
		HUDController:SetResource("Power", `{math.floor(needed + 0.5)}/{math.floor(made + 0.5)}`, lamp)
	end
	for _, name in { "PowerMade", "PowerNeeded", "DarkRooms" } do
		RunState.Changed(name):Connect(showPower)
	end
	showPower()
	-- the stockpile (EconomyService replicates the amounts as RunState values)
	for _, entry in STOCK do
		if RunState.Fields[entry.Id] then
			local function show()
				local value = RunState.Get(entry.Id)
				HUDController:SetResource(entry.Id, if type(value) == "number" then tostring(value) else "—")
			end
			RunState.Changed(entry.Id):Connect(show)
			show()
		end
	end
	-- messages from the server for the alert feed (a refused proposal, a room built...)
	Remotes.OnClient("Alert", function(kind: any, text: any)
		if type(text) == "string" then
			HUDController:Alert(if kind == "Danger" or kind == "Warning" then kind else "Info", text)
		end
	end)

	-- the clock
	RunState.Changed("Year"):Connect(showYear)
	RunState.Changed("Era"):Connect(showEra)
	RunState.Changed("Siren"):Connect(onSiren)
	RunState.Changed("CyclePhase"):Connect(onPhase)
	RunState.Changed("RunPhase"):Connect(refreshVisible)
	showYear()
	showEra()
	-- Disturbance (Prompt 14)
	RunState.Changed("Disturbance"):Connect(showDisturbance)
	RunState.Changed("TremorAt"):Connect(function()
		seismoTremorUntil = os.clock() + 2.5
	end)
	showDisturbance()
	local seismoElapsed = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function(dt: number)
		seismoElapsed += dt
		if seismoElapsed >= 1 / SEISMO_HZ and gui and gui.Enabled then
			tickSeismograph(seismoElapsed)
			seismoElapsed = 0
		end
	end)
	local elapsed = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function(dt: number)
		elapsed += dt
		if elapsed >= TICK_SECONDS and gui and gui.Enabled then
			elapsed = 0
			tickClock()
		end
	end)
	local function pressReady()
		if Remotes.InPlace("SetReady") and part("Ready").Visible then
			Remotes.FireServer("SetReady", Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("Ready") ~= true)
		end
	end
	part("Ready").Activated:Connect(pressReady)
	input:On("Ready", pressReady)

	-- health, the ability, the hotbar, the Command View
	Players.LocalPlayer.CharacterAdded:Connect(watchHealth)
	if Players.LocalPlayer.Character then
		task.spawn(watchHealth, Players.LocalPlayer.Character)
	end
	part("Vitals.Ability").Activated:Connect(function()
		input:Press("Ability", true, "HudAbility")
		input:Press("Ability", false, "HudAbility")
	end)
	for i = 1, 5 do
		input:On(`Hotbar{i}`, function()
			HUDController:SelectSlot(i)
		end)
		part(`Hotbar.Slot{i}`).Activated:Connect(function()
			HUDController:SelectSlot(i)
		end)
	end
	input:On("HotbarNext", function()
		HUDController:SelectSlot(selectedSlot % 5 + 1)
	end)
	input:On("HotbarPrevious", function()
		HUDController:SelectSlot((selectedSlot - 2) % 5 + 1)
	end)
	input:BindButton("CommandView", part("CommandView"))
	-- PC: the camera locks the mouse; a click of the mouse wheel frees the cursor to click the
	-- HUD (and the vote telegram), and another click locks it again (Landon, 2026-11-08)
	UserInputService.InputBegan:Connect(function(io: InputObject)
		if io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton3 then
			cursorFree = not cursorFree
			camera:FreeCursor("HudCursor", cursorFree)
		end
	end)

	-- the ore chips show once the team has dug into that ore's band (Landon, 2026-11-08)
	replica:Changed("Cells"):Connect(refreshOreChips)
	refreshOreChips()

	-- menus hide the HUD (and take back a cursor the wheel freed: the menu frees its own)
	ui.Opened:Connect(function()
		HUDController:Hide("Frame", true)
		if cursorFree then
			cursorFree = false
			camera:FreeCursor("HudCursor", false)
		end
	end)
	ui.Closed:Connect(function()
		HUDController:Hide("Frame", false)
	end)
	refreshVisible()
	tickClock()
	log:Debug("HUD ready")
end

return HUDController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000063"><Properties><string name="Name">InputController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	InputController: turns PC, touch and gamepad input into the game's actions (bible Section 9,
	Controls; Section 23).

	* Device: "Keyboard" (mouse and keyboard), "Gamepad" or "Touch", from the last input used;
	  DeviceChanged fires when it changes.
	* Actions: the bible's controls table (BINDINGS). A controller listens with
	  InputController:On(action, began, ended?); the action is bound with ContextActionService
	  above Roblox's own bindings the first time someone listens. Touch buttons from the HUD
	  join with InputController:BindButton(action, button). Jump and moving stay Roblox's.
	* Look and zoom: mouse movement (while the mouse is locked), the right stick, a one-finger
	  drag on open screen and a two-finger pinch are gathered between frames; the camera takes
	  them with TakeLook(dt) (degrees) and TakeZoom() (studs, positive = farther).
	* Touches that start on a GUI or Roblox's thumbstick are the GUI's, never the camera's.
	* Block(reason, true) holds gameplay actions off while a menu is open: new presses are
	  ignored and anything held is released. Command View still passes, so its key can close
	  the docked Frame.
]]

local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local CameraRig = require(Shared.Rules.CameraRig)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)

local log = Log.new("InputController")

export type Device = "Keyboard" | "Gamepad" | "Touch"

-- Section 9's controls table. Touch buttons come from the HUD (BindButton).
local BINDINGS: { [string]: { Enum.KeyCode | Enum.UserInputType } } = {
	Fire = { Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton1, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR2 },
	Aim = { Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton2, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL2 },
	Melee = { Enum.KeyCode.F, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR1 },
	Reload = { Enum.KeyCode.R, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonX }, -- a tap of X on console
	Interact = { Enum.KeyCode.E, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonX }, -- a hold of X on console
	Ability = { Enum.KeyCode.Q, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL1 },
	Sprint = { Enum.KeyCode.LeftShift, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL3 },
	Dodge = { Enum.KeyCode.LeftControl, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonB },
	SwapShoulder = { Enum.KeyCode.V, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR3 },
	HotbarNext = { Enum.KeyCode.DPadRight },
	HotbarPrevious = { Enum.KeyCode.DPadLeft },
	Hotbar1 = { Enum.KeyCode.One },
	Hotbar2 = { Enum.KeyCode.Two },
	Hotbar3 = { Enum.KeyCode.Three },
	Hotbar4 = { Enum.KeyCode.Four },
	Hotbar5 = { Enum.KeyCode.Five },
	Ping = { Enum.KeyCode.G }, -- and a tap of D-pad up (TAP_HOLD)
	Heal = { Enum.KeyCode.H }, -- Landon, 2026-11-08: and a hold of D-pad up (TAP_HOLD)
	CommandView = { Enum.KeyCode.Tab, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonSelect },
	Ready = { Enum.KeyCode.Z, Enum.KeyCode.DPadDown }, -- Landon, 2026-11-08: Ready gets its own key
	Vote = { Enum.KeyCode.ButtonY }, -- Landon, 2026-11-08: votes on a controller (tap yes, hold no)
}
-- One gamepad button, two actions: a tap does one, a hold past TapHoldSeconds the other.
-- D-pad up pings on a tap (Section 9's controls) and heals on a hold (Landon, 2026-11-08).
local TAP_HOLD: { [Enum.KeyCode]: { Tap: string, Hold: string } } = {
	[Enum.KeyCode.DPadUp] = { Tap = "Ping", Hold = "Heal" },
}
local PRIORITY = Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 10
local NEVER_BLOCKED: { [string]: boolean } = { CommandView = true, Vote = true } -- a vote can be answered from any screen
-- Keys the engine marks as processed before ContextActionService sees them begin (Tab: Roblox
-- keeps it for its player list and UI navigation; the gamepad's View button: Roblox's own UI
-- selection, which Init turns off). These are read from UserInputService too, unless a text box
-- has focus or Roblox's menu is open.
local PROCESSED_KEYS: { [Enum.KeyCode]: string } =
	{ [Enum.KeyCode.Tab] = "CommandView", [Enum.KeyCode.ButtonSelect] = "CommandView" }

type Listener = { Began: (() -> ())?, Ended: (() -> ())? }

local InputController = {
	Name = "InputController",
	Dependencies = {},
	DeviceChanged = Signal.new(),
}

local device: Device = "Keyboard"
local listeners: { [string]: { Listener } } = {}
local held: { [string]: { [any]: boolean } } = {}
local bound: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local blocked: { [string]: boolean } = {}

local mouseLook = Vector2.zero -- pixels since the last TakeLook
local touchLook = Vector2.zero
local stick = Vector2.zero -- the right stick, -1 to 1
local zoom = 0 -- studs since the last TakeZoom
local touches: { [InputObject]: Vector2 } = {} -- camera touches and where they were last
local pinchGap: number? = nil

-- The player's own Roblox camera sensitivity (Settings menu), read each frame.
local gameSettings: any = nil
local function robloxSensitivity(key: string): number
	if not gameSettings then
		return 1
	end
	local ok, value = pcall(function()
		return gameSettings[key]
	end)
	return if ok and type(value) == "number" and value > 0 then value else 1
end

local function deviceOf(inputType: Enum.UserInputType): Device?
	if inputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch then
		return "Touch"
	elseif string.find(inputType.Name, "^Gamepad") then
		return "Gamepad"
	elseif inputType == Enum.UserInputType.Keyboard or string.find(inputType.Name, "^Mouse") then
		return "Keyboard"
	end
	return nil
end

local function setDevice(inputType: Enum.UserInputType)
	local found = deviceOf(inputType)
	if found and found ~= device then
		device = found
		InputController.DeviceChanged:Fire(device)
	end
end

-- An action's state from one source (a key, a button); began on the first, ended on the last.
local function press(action: string, source: any, down: boolean)
	local sources = held[action]
	if not sources then
		sources = {}
		held[action] = sources
	end
	local wasDown = next(sources) ~= nil
	if down and not wasDown and next(blocked) ~= nil and not NEVER_BLOCKED[action] then
		return
	end
	sources[source] = if down then true else nil
	local isDown = next(sources) ~= nil
	if isDown == wasDown then
		return
	end
	for _, listener in listeners[action] or {} do
		local handler = if isDown then listener.Began else listener.Ended
		if handler then
			task.spawn(handler)
		end
	end
end

local tapHoldBound: { [Enum.KeyCode]: boolean } = {}
local function bindTapHold(key: Enum.KeyCode)
	local pair = TAP_HOLD[key]
	if tapHoldBound[key] or not pair then
		return
	end
	tapHoldBound[key] = true
	local downAt: number? = nil
	local holding = false
	local source = "TapHold" .. key.Name
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(
		"100Y_TapHold_" .. key.Name,
		function(_name: string, state: Enum.UserInputState, _input: InputObject): Enum.ContextActionResult
			if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
				local at = os.clock()
				downAt = at
				holding = false
				local seconds = 0.35
				local ok, tuning = pcall(function()
					return require(Shared.Config).Get("Tuning", "Combat")
				end)
				if ok and tuning and tuning.TapHoldSeconds then
					seconds = tuning.TapHoldSeconds
				end
				task.delay(seconds, function()
					if downAt == at then
						holding = true
						press(pair.Hold, source, true)
					end
				end)
			elseif state == Enum.UserInputState.End or state == Enum.UserInputState.Cancel then
				local wasDown = downAt ~= nil
				downAt = nil
				if holding then
					holding = false
					press(pair.Hold, source, false)
				elseif wasDown and state == Enum.UserInputState.End then
					press(pair.Tap, source, true)
					press(pair.Tap, source, false)
				end
			end
			return Enum.ContextActionResult.Pass
		end,
		false,
		PRIORITY,
		key
	)
end

local function bind(action: string)
	local inputs = BINDINGS[action]
	if bound[action] or not inputs then
		return
	end
	for key, pair in TAP_HOLD do
		if pair.Tap == action or pair.Hold == action then
			bindTapHold(key)
		end
	end
	bound[action] = true
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(
		"100Y_" .. action,
		function(_name: string, state: Enum.UserInputState, input: InputObject): Enum.ContextActionResult
			if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
				press(action, input.KeyCode.Name .. input.UserInputType.Name, true)
			elseif state == Enum.UserInputState.End or state == Enum.UserInputState.Cancel then
				press(action, input.KeyCode.Name .. input.UserInputType.Name, false)
			end
			return Enum.ContextActionResult.Pass
		end,
		false,
		PRIORITY,
		table.unpack(inputs)
	)
end

-- Listens to an action. Returns a function that stops listening.
function InputController:On(action: string, began: (() -> ())?, ended: (() -> ())?): () -> ()
	assert(BINDINGS[action], `InputController: unknown action {action}`)
	local list = listeners[action]
	if not list then
		list = {}
		listeners[action] = list
	end
	local listener: Listener = { Began = began, Ended = ended }
	table.insert(list, listener)
	bind(action)
	return function()
		local index = table.find(list, listener)
		if index then
			table.remove(list, index)
		end
	end
end

-- Is the action held right now (by any key, button or touch button)?
function InputController:IsDown(action: string): boolean
	local sources = held[action]
	return sources ~= nil and next(sources) ~= nil
end

-- A HUD touch button drives an action while it is pressed. Returns a cleanup function.
function InputController:BindButton(action: string, button: GuiButton): () -> ()
	assert(BINDINGS[action], `InputController: unknown action {action}`)
	local down = button.MouseButton1Down:Connect(function()
		press(action, button, true)
	end)
	local up = button.MouseButton1Up:Connect(function()
		press(action, button, false)
	end)
	local left = button.MouseLeave:Connect(function()
		press(action, button, false)
	end)
	return function()
		down:Disconnect()
		up:Disconnect()
		left:Disconnect()
		press(action, button, false)
	end
end

-- Presses or releases an action from code (DevTools, tests, a toggle on touch).
function InputController:Press(action: string, down: boolean, source: string?)
	assert(BINDINGS[action], `InputController: unknown action {action}`)
	press(action, source or "code", down)
end

function InputController:Device(): Device
	return device
end

-- Holds gameplay actions off while a menu is open (reason: the menu's name).
function InputController:Block(reason: string, on: boolean)
	blocked[reason] = if on then true else nil
	if on then
		for action, sources in held do
			if not NEVER_BLOCKED[action] then
				for source in sources do
					press(action, source, false)
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

function InputController:IsBlocked(): boolean
	return next(blocked) ~= nil
end

-- Look input since the last call, in degrees (X turns, Y tilts; positive = right and down).
function InputController:TakeLook(dt: number): Vector2
	local t = CameraRig.Tuning()
	local degrees = mouseLook * t.MouseDegreesPerPixel * robloxSensitivity("MouseSensitivity")
		+ touchLook * t.TouchDegreesPerPixel * robloxSensitivity("MouseSensitivity")
		+ CameraRig.Stick(stick, t.StickDeadzone) * Vector2.new(1, -1) * t.GamepadDegreesPerSecond * dt
			* robloxSensitivity("GamepadCameraSensitivity")
	mouseLook = Vector2.zero
	touchLook = Vector2.zero
	return degrees
end

-- Zoom input since the last call, in studs (positive = farther).
function InputController:TakeZoom(): number
	local value = zoom
	zoom = 0
	return value
end

function InputController:Init()
	local ok, settings = pcall(function()
		return UserSettings():GetService("UserGameSettings")
	end)
	gameSettings = if ok then settings else nil
	device = deviceOf(UserInputService:GetLastInputType())
		or (if UserInputService.TouchEnabled and not UserInputService.KeyboardEnabled then "Touch" else "Keyboard")
	-- The View button opens the Command View (bible Section 7); with this on, Roblox takes that
	-- button for its own UI selection. Our screens select for the gamepad themselves (UIController).
	GuiService.AutoSelectGuiEnabled = false
end

function InputController:Start()
	UserInputService.LastInputTypeChanged:Connect(setDevice)
	UserInputService.InputBegan:Connect(function(io: InputObject, processed: boolean)
		local action = PROCESSED_KEYS[io.KeyCode]
		if action and processed and bound[action] and not UserInputService:GetFocusedTextBox() and not GuiService.MenuIsOpen then
			press(action, "Processed" .. io.KeyCode.Name, true)
		end
	end)
	UserInputService.InputEnded:Connect(function(io: InputObject)
		local action = PROCESSED_KEYS[io.KeyCode]
		if action then
			press(action, "Processed" .. io.KeyCode.Name, false)
		end
	end)

	UserInputService.InputChanged:Connect(function(input: InputObject, processed: boolean)
		if input.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseMovement then
			if UserInputService.MouseBehavior ~= Enum.MouseBehavior.Default then
				mouseLook += Vector2.new(input.Delta.X, input.Delta.Y)
			end
		elseif input.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseWheel then
			if not processed then
				zoom -= input.Position.Z * CameraRig.Tuning().ZoomStep
			end
		elseif input.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick2 then
			stick = Vector2.new(input.Position.X, input.Position.Y)
		end
	end)
	UserInputService.InputEnded:Connect(function(input: InputObject)
		if input.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick2 then
			stick = Vector2.zero
		end
	end)

	-- Touch: a drag on open screen looks around; two fingers pinch to zoom.
	UserInputService.TouchStarted:Connect(function(touch: InputObject, processed: boolean)
		if not processed then
			touches[touch] = Vector2.new(touch.Position.X, touch.Position.Y)
			pinchGap = nil
		end
	end)
	UserInputService.TouchMoved:Connect(function(touch: InputObject)
		local last = touches[touch]
		if not last then
			return
		end
		local now = Vector2.new(touch.Position.X, touch.Position.Y)
		touches[touch] = now
		local live = {}
		for other, at in touches do
			table.insert(live, at)
		end
		if #live >= 2 then
			local gap = (live[1] - live[2]).Magnitude
			if pinchGap then
				zoom -= (gap - pinchGap) * CameraRig.Tuning().PinchStudsPerPixel
			end
			pinchGap = gap
		else
			touchLook += now - last
		end
	end)
	UserInputService.TouchEnded:Connect(function(touch: InputObject)
		touches[touch] = nil
		pinchGap = nil
	end)
	log:Debug("input ready (%s)", device)
end

return InputController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000064"><Properties><string name="Name">MiniMapController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	MiniMapController: the side-view mini-map on the HUD (bible Section 18: "a side-view
	mini-map of the bunker with alerts blinking").

	It draws a window of the bunker around the player (Rules.Hud.MapWindow: 5 columns, 5 floors)
	from the replicated Cells and Rooms collections: each room as one block across its cells with
	its short name, a dug cell as a faint block, rock as bare blueprint paper. The player's cell
	lights an orange pilot lamp. The footer names the deepest band and floor reached.
	Pinged cells (PingService, from the Command View) show a yellow pin for Tuning.Ping.Seconds.
	Blink(roomId, on) is for the alerts (AlertController, Prompt 12).
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Hud = require(Shared.Rules.Hud)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)

local log = Log.new("MiniMapController")

local COLUMNS = 5
local ROWS = 5
local INSET = 0.05 -- of a cell, on each side
local POLL_SECONDS = 0.25
local NAVY = Color3.fromHex("#1B2A3A")
local RUST = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B")

local MiniMapController = {
	Name = "MiniMapController",
	Dependencies = { "ReplicaController", "HUDController" },
}

local replica: any = nil
local hud: any = nil
local cellsFrame: Frame? = nil
local you: ImageLabel? = nil
local depthLabel: TextLabel? = nil
local template: Frame? = nil
local playerCell: { number }? = nil
local dirty = true
local blinking: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local blocks: { [string]: Frame } = {}
local window = { 0, 1 } -- the first column and first floor shown
local pingTemplate: Instance? = nil
local pingMarks: { { Frame: any, Floor: number, Column: number, Until: number } } = {}

local function placePings()
	local now = os.clock()
	for i = #pingMarks, 1, -1 do
		local ping = pingMarks[i]
		if now > ping.Until then
			ping.Frame:Destroy()
			table.remove(pingMarks, i)
		else
			local x = (ping.Column - window[1] + 0.5) / COLUMNS
			local y = (ping.Floor - window[2] + 0.75) / ROWS
			ping.Frame.Position = UDim2.fromScale(x, y)
			ping.Frame.Visible = x > 0 and x < 1 and y > 0 and y <= 1
		end
	end
end

local function shortName(roomType: string): string
	local room = Config.Find("Rooms", roomType)
	local name = if room then room.Name else roomType
	return string.upper(string.match(name, "^(%S+)") or name)
end

local function block(key: string, floor: number, column: number, span: number, first: { number }, label: string, dug: boolean)
	local frame = (template :: Frame):Clone()
	frame.Name = key
	frame.Visible = true
	local c0, f0 = first[1], first[2]
	local from = math.max(column, c0)
	local to = math.min(column + span - 1, c0 + COLUMNS - 1)
	frame.Position = UDim2.fromScale((from - c0 + INSET) / COLUMNS, (floor - f0 + INSET) / ROWS)
	frame.Size = UDim2.fromScale((to - from + 1 - 2 * INSET) / COLUMNS, (1 - 2 * INSET) / ROWS)
	frame.BackgroundTransparency = if dug then 0.85 else 0.55
	frame.BackgroundColor3 = if blinking[key] then RUST else NAVY
	local text = frame:FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel?
	if text then
		text.Text = label
		text.Visible = label ~= "" and (to - from + 1) >= 1
	end
	frame.Parent = cellsFrame
	blocks[key] = frame
end

local function redraw()
	dirty = false
	local holder = cellsFrame
	if not holder or not template then
		return
	end
	for _, child in holder:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			child:Destroy()
		end
	end
	table.clear(blocks)
	local grid = Grid.Tuning()
	local here = playerCell or { 1, 0 }
	local c0, f0 = Hud.MapWindow(here[1], here[2], grid, COLUMNS, ROWS)
	local first = { c0, f0 }
	window = first
	local seenRooms: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	local deepest = 0
	for key, cell in replica:All("Cells") do
		local floor, column = Grid.Parse(key)
		if floor and column then
			deepest = math.max(deepest, floor)
			if floor >= f0 and floor < f0 + ROWS and column >= c0 and column < c0 + COLUMNS then
				local roomId = if type(cell) == "table" then cell.Room else nil
				if roomId then
					if not seenRooms[roomId] then
						seenRooms[roomId] = true
						local room = replica:Get("Rooms", roomId)
						if room then
							block(roomId, room.Floor, room.Column, room.Span or 1, first, shortName(room.Type), false)
						end
					end
				else
					block(key, floor, column, 1, first, "", true)
				end
			end
		end
	end
	if you then
		you.Visible = playerCell ~= nil
		if playerCell then
			you.Position = UDim2.fromScale((playerCell[2] - c0 + 0.5) / COLUMNS, (playerCell[1] - f0 + 0.5) / ROWS)
		end
	end
	if depthLabel then
		if deepest > 0 then
			local band = Grid.BandOf(deepest)
			depthLabel.Text = `{string.upper(band.Name)}  ·  DEPTH {deepest}`
		else
			depthLabel.Text = ""
		end
	end
end

local function poll()
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	local floor, column = nil, nil
	if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then
		floor, column = Grid.CellAt(root.Position)
	end
	local cell = if floor and column then { floor, column } else nil
	local changed = (cell == nil) ~= (playerCell == nil)
		or (cell ~= nil and playerCell ~= nil and (cell[1] ~= playerCell[1] or cell[2] ~= playerCell[2]))
	if changed then
		playerCell = cell
		dirty = true
	end
	if dirty then
		redraw()
	end
	placePings()
end

-- Shows a pin on a cell for Tuning.Ping.Seconds (PingService's CellPinged).
function MiniMapController:Ping(floor: number, column: number)
	if not cellsFrame or not pingTemplate then
		return
	end
	local mark = pingTemplate:Clone() :: any
	mark.Visible = true
	mark.Parent = cellsFrame.Parent
	table.insert(pingMarks, { Frame = mark, Floor = floor, Column = column, Until = os.clock() + Config.Get("Tuning", "Ping").Seconds })
	placePings()
end

-- Lights a room's block (or a dug cell's, by "floor,column") rust red while on.
function MiniMapController:Blink(key: string, on: boolean)
	blinking[key] = if on then true else nil
	local frame = blocks[key]
	if frame then
		frame.BackgroundColor3 = if on then RUST else NAVY
	end
end

function MiniMapController:Init(registry)
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	hud = registry.HUDController
end

function MiniMapController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	local gui = hud:Gui()
	local waited = 0
	while not gui and waited < 20 do -- HUDController finds the HUD in its own Start
		waited += task.wait(0.25)
		gui = hud:Gui()
	end
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local paper = gui:FindFirstChild("MiniMap") and gui.MiniMap:FindFirstChild("Paper")
	cellsFrame = paper and paper:FindFirstChild("Cells")
	you = paper and paper:FindFirstChild("You")
	depthLabel = gui.MiniMap:FindFirstChild("Depth")
	template = gui:FindFirstChild("Templates") and gui.Templates:FindFirstChild("MapCell")
	if not cellsFrame or not template then
		log:Warn("the HUD has no mini-map")
		return
	end
	pingTemplate = gui.Templates:FindFirstChild("MapPing")
	if Remotes.InPlace("CellPinged") then
		Remotes.OnClient("CellPinged", function(floor: any, column: any)
			if type(floor) == "number" and type(column) == "number" then
				MiniMapController:Ping(floor, column)
			end
		end)
	end
	local function mark()
		dirty = true
	end
	replica:Changed("Cells"):Connect(mark)
	replica:Changed("Rooms"):Connect(mark)
	task.spawn(function()
		while true do
			poll()
			task.wait(POLL_SECONDS)
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("mini-map ready")
end

return MiniMapController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000065"><Properties><string name="Name">NPCAnimator</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	NPCAnimator: plays residents' (and later monsters') animations from replicated state (bible
	Section 23: animations play on clients from a replicated Activity attribute, which keeps the
	server light and avoids Animate scripts in NPCs). Run place only.

	It watches workspace.Bunker.Residents and workspace.Monsters (Prompt 12). For each model, the
	clip in Config.Animations whose Rig (the model's Rig attribute; residents are R15) and
	Activity match its Activity attribute plays, looped as the clip says; any other activity
	stops it. Fleeing and running use the walk when there is no clip of their own. A monster's
	attack replays each time its AttackAt attribute changes. Today there are the residents' walk
	(A0) and the monsters' A4 clips; A3 adds working, eating and sleeping with no code change.
]]

local ContentProvider = game:GetService("ContentProvider")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)

local log = Log.new("NPCAnimator")

local NPCAnimator = {
	Name = "NPCAnimator",
	Dependencies = {},
}

type Watched = { Tracks: { [string]: AnimationTrack }, Playing: AnimationTrack?, Connections: { RBXScriptConnection } }

local watched: { [Model]: Watched } = {}
local clips: { [string]: any } = {} -- "Rig:Activity" -> Config.Animations entry
-- Activities without a clip of their own borrow one: residents beating out a fire (Prompt 13)
-- kneel and work like a player reviving, until A3 brings their own clip.
local FALLBACK: { [string]: string } = { Flee = "Walk", Run = "Walk", Fight = "Attack", Extinguish = "Revive" }

local function rigOf(model: Model): string
	local rig = model:GetAttribute("Rig")
	return if type(rig) == "string" then rig else "R15"
end

local function clipFor(model: Model, activity: string): (any, string)
	local rig = rigOf(model)
	local clip = clips[`{rig}:{activity}`]
	if not clip and FALLBACK[activity] then
		activity = FALLBACK[activity]
		clip = clips[`{rig}:{activity}`]
	end
	return clip, activity
end

local function trackFor(model: Model, state: Watched, wanted: string): AnimationTrack?
	local clip, activity = clipFor(model, wanted)
	if not clip then
		return nil
	end
	local existing = state.Tracks[activity]
	if existing then
		return existing
	end
	local humanoid = model:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	local animator = humanoid and humanoid:FindFirstChildOfClass("Animator")
	if not animator then
		return nil
	end
	local animation = Instance.new("Animation")
	animation.AnimationId = clip.AssetId
	local ok, track = pcall(function()
		return (animator :: Animator):LoadAnimation(animation)
	end)
	if not ok or not track then
		log:Warn("couldn't load %s for %s: %s", clip.AssetId, model.Name, tostring(track))
		return nil
	end
	track.Looped = clip.Looped
	state.Tracks[activity] = track
	return track
end

local function apply(model: Model)
	local state = watched[model]
	if not state then
		return
	end
	local activity = model:GetAttribute("Activity")
	local track = if type(activity) == "string" then trackFor(model, state, activity) else nil
	if state.Playing and state.Playing ~= track then
		state.Playing:Stop(0.2)
		state.Playing = nil
	end
	if track and not track.IsPlaying then
		track:Play(0.2)
		state.Playing = track
	end
end

local function watch(model: Instance)
	if not model:IsA("Model") or watched[model] then
		return
	end
	local state: Watched = { Tracks = {}, Playing = nil, Connections = {} }
	watched[model] = state
	table.insert(state.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Activity"):Connect(function()
		apply(model)
	end))
	-- a monster's attack replays on every AttackAt
	table.insert(state.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("AttackAt"):Connect(function()
		local track = trackFor(model, state, "Attack")
		if track then
			if state.Playing and state.Playing ~= track then
				state.Playing:Stop(0.1)
			end
			track:Play(0.05)
			state.Playing = track
		end
	end))
	table.insert(state.Connections, model.AncestryChanged:Connect(function(_, parent)
		if parent == nil then
			for _, connection in state.Connections do
				connection:Disconnect()
			end
			watched[model] = nil
		end
	end))
	-- the Animator arrives from the server with the body
	task.defer(apply, model)
end

function NPCAnimator:Init() end

function NPCAnimator:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	local ids = {}
	for _, clip in Config.All("Animations") do
		clips[`{clip.Rig}:{clip.Activity}`] = clip
		table.insert(ids, clip.AssetId)
	end
	task.spawn(function()
		local animations = {}
		for _, id in ids do
			local animation = Instance.new("Animation")
			animation.AnimationId = id
			table.insert(animations, animation)
		end
		pcall(function()
			ContentProvider:PreloadAsync(animations)
		end)
	end)
	task.spawn(function()
		local bunker = workspace:WaitForChild("Bunker", 60)
		local holder = bunker and bunker:WaitForChild("Residents", 60)
		if not holder then
			log:Warn("no workspace.Bunker.Residents: residents won't animate")
			return
		end
		for _, model in holder:GetChildren() do
			watch(model)
		end
		holder.ChildAdded:Connect(watch)
		log:Debug("watching residents (%d clips)", #ids)
	end)
	task.spawn(function()
		local monsters = workspace:WaitForChild("Monsters", 120)
		if not monsters then
			return
		end
		for _, model in monsters:GetChildren() do
			watch(model)
		end
		monsters.ChildAdded:Connect(watch)
	end)
end

return NPCAnimator
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000066"><Properties><string name="Name">ReplicaController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ReplicaController: the client end of the delta channel. It mirrors the server's
	collections (ReplicationService) and tells controllers what changed.

		local Rooms = registry.ReplicaController
		Rooms:Changed("Rooms"):Connect(function(key, value, old) ... end)  -- value nil = removed
		local room = Rooms:Get("Rooms", "R12")                              -- frozen; never edit
		Rooms:Ready():Wait()                                                -- first snapshot in

	A snapshot replaces the whole mirror: keys that disappeared fire a removal.
	A collection cleared on the server fires one change with key nil.
]]

local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Delta = require(Shared.Utilities.Delta)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)

local log = Log.new("ReplicaController")

export type ChangedSignal = Signal.Signal<string?, any, any>

local ReplicaController = {
	Name = "ReplicaController",
	Dependencies = {},
}

local store: Delta.Store = {}
local changedSignals: { [string]: ChangedSignal } = {}
local readySignal = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<()>
local isReady = false
local counters = { Events = 0, Ops = 0, Snapshots = 0 }

local function onDelta(ops: any, snapshot: any)
	if type(ops) ~= "table" then
		return
	end
	counters.Events += 1
	counters.Ops += #ops
	local changes: { Delta.Change }
	if snapshot == true then
		counters.Snapshots += 1
		local previous = store
		store = {}
		changes = Delta.Apply(store, ops)
		for _, change in changes do
			local before = previous[change.Collection]
			change.Old = if before and change.Key then before[change.Key] else nil
		end
		for collectionName, values in previous do
			local now = store[collectionName]
			for key, value in values do
				if not now or now[key] == nil then
					table.insert(changes, { Collection = collectionName, Key = key, Value = nil, Old = value })
				end
			end
		end
	else
		changes = Delta.Apply(store, ops)
	end
	for _, change in changes do
		local signal = changedSignals[change.Collection]
		if signal then
			signal:Fire(change.Key, change.Value, change.Old)
		end
	end
	if snapshot == true and not isReady then
		isReady = true
		log:Debug("snapshot: %d values", #ops)
		readySignal:Fire()
	end
end

function ReplicaController:Init(_registry)
	Remotes.OnClient("Delta", onDelta)
end

function ReplicaController:Get(collection: string, key: string): any
	local values = store[collection]
	return if values then values[key] else nil
end

-- A shallow copy of a collection (the values are frozen).
function ReplicaController:All(collection: string): { [string]: any }
	local values = store[collection]
	return if values then table.clone(values) else {}
end

function ReplicaController:Changed(collection: string): ChangedSignal
	local signal = changedSignals[collection]
	if not signal then
		signal = Signal.new() :: ChangedSignal
		changedSignals[collection] = signal
	end
	return signal :: ChangedSignal
end

function ReplicaController:IsReady(): boolean
	return isReady
end

-- Fires once, after the first snapshot. Check IsReady first: it won't fire again.
function ReplicaController:Ready(): Signal.Signal<()>
	return readySignal
end

function ReplicaController:Stats(): { Events: number, Ops: number, Snapshots: number }
	return table.clone(counters)
end

return ReplicaController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000067"><Properties><string name="Name">ResidentsController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ResidentsController: the Residents screen (bible Section 18: "Residents (run) | All, by job,
	idle, injured, away | Resident cards | Resident card; Assign"), phase 1. Run place only. It
	opens from the Command View's footer (RESIDENTS) and from DevTools.

	* Tabs: All, Working (by job), Idle, Hurt (hurt or down). Away comes with expeditions
	  (Prompt 18).
	* A card per resident: the name, the job and level, the Common enamel. The portrait is the
	  Survivor's outfit until A3 brings the resident kit.
	* The resident card (zone D): job, stats, needs (health, rest, morale), experience to the next
	  level and the run log.
	* The main action: Assign (an idle resident goes to the free job that suits their best stat,
	  Section 7's Auto-Assign rule for one person) or Take off the job. The footer: Auto-Assign
	  (every idle resident).
	Everything comes from the Residents and Rooms collections; the server checks every change.
]]

local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local UIKit = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local log = Log.new("ResidentsController")

local ResidentsController = {
	Name = "ResidentsController",
	Dependencies = { "UIController", "ReplicaController" },
}

local ui: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local page: any = nil
local selected: string? = nil
local tab = "All"

local STATS = { "Strength", "Smarts", "Grit", "Speed", "Charm" }

local function roomName(roomType: string): string
	local info = Config.Find("Rooms", roomType)
	return if info then info.Name else roomType
end

local function jobOf(resident: any): (string?, string?)
	local room = if resident.Job then replica:Get("Rooms", resident.Job) else nil
	if not room then
		return nil, nil
	end
	return roomName(room.Type), Config.Get("Rooms", room.Type).WorkerStat
end

local function best(resident: any): string
	local id, value = "Strength", -1
	for _, stat in STATS do
		if (resident.Stats[stat] or 0) > value then
			id, value = stat, resident.Stats[stat] or 0
		end
	end
	return id
end

-- The free job that suits a resident: a room with a free slot whose job uses their highest stat.
local function bestJob(resident: any): string?
	local used: { [string]: number } = {}
	for _, other in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(other) == "table" and other.Job and other.State ~= "Dead" then
			used[other.Job] = (used[other.Job] or 0) + 1
		end
	end
	local pick, pickValue = nil, -1
	for id, room in replica:All("Rooms") do
		local stat = Config.Get("Rooms", room.Type).WorkerStat
		if stat then
			local slots = Config.Get("Tuning", "Rooms").WorkerSlotsPerCell[room.Level] * room.Span
			local value = resident.Stats[stat] or 0
			if (used[id] or 0) < slots and value > pickValue then
				pick, pickValue = id, value
			end
		end
	end
	return pick
end

local function section(body: Instance, order: number, label: string, text: string)
	local s = ui:Clone("Section")
	s.LayoutOrder = order
	s.Label.Text = string.upper(label)
	s.Body.Text = text
	s.Parent = body
end

local function portrait(): string?
	return if UIKit.Sprites["Portrait_Survivor"] then "Portrait_Survivor" else nil
end

local function showResident(id: string)
	local resident = replica:Get("Residents", id)
	local detail: any = page:FindFirstChild("Detail")
	if not resident then
		detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "NOBODY"
		detail.Sub.Text = ""
		ui:Clear(detail.Body)
		ui:SetMainAction(nil)
		return
	end
	local hero = portrait()
	local heroImage: any = detail.Hero:FindFirstChild("Image")
	heroImage.Visible = hero ~= nil
	if hero then
		ui:SetSprite(heroImage, hero)
	end
	ui:SetRarity(detail, if resident.Tier == "Free" then "Common" else resident.Tier)
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(resident.Name)
	detail.Sub.Text = `LEVEL {resident.Level}  ·  AGE {resident.Age}`
	local body = ui:Clear(detail.Body)
	local job, stat = jobOf(resident)
	section(body, 1, "Job", if resident.State == "Down" then "Down: revive them with a Medkit before it's too late."
		elseif job then `{job}, on {stat} {resident.Stats[stat or ""] or 0}.`
		else `Idle. Best at {best(resident)} ({resident.Stats[best(resident)]}).`)
	local stats = {}
	for _, s in STATS do
		table.insert(stats, `{s} {resident.Stats[s]}`)
	end
	section(body, 2, "Stats", table.concat(stats, "  ·  "))
	section(body, 3, "Needs", `Health {resident.Health} of {resident.MaxHealth}  ·  Rest {resident.Rest}  ·  Morale {resident.Morale} ({resident.Mood})`
		.. (if resident.Hungry then "  ·  Hungry" else ""))
	section(body, 4, "Experience", `{resident.XP} of {resident.XPNext} to level {resident.Level + 1}`)
	local history = resident.Log or {}
	local lines = {}
	for i = math.max(1, #history - 3), #history do
		table.insert(lines, history[i])
	end
	section(body, 5, "Run log", if #lines > 0 then table.concat(lines, "\n") else "Nothing yet.")
	if resident.State ~= "Alive" then
		ui:SetMainAction({ Label = "Down", Enabled = false })
	elseif resident.Job then
		ui:SetMainAction({
			Label = "Take off the job",
			Enabled = true,
			OnPress = function()
				Remotes.FireServer("AssignResident", id, "")
			end,
		})
	else
		local roomId = bestJob(resident)
		ui:SetMainAction({
			Label = "Assign",
			Enabled = roomId ~= nil,
			OnPress = function()
				if roomId then
					Remotes.FireServer("AssignResident", id, roomId)
				end
			end,
		})
	end
end

local function wanted(resident: any): boolean
	if resident.State == "Dead" then
		return false
	end
	if tab == "Working" then
		return resident.Job ~= nil
	elseif tab == "Idle" then
		return resident.Job == nil and resident.State == "Alive"
	elseif tab == "Hurt" then
		return resident.State == "Down" or resident.Health < resident.MaxHealth
	end
	return true
end

local function fill()
	if not page then
		return
	end
	local content: any = page:FindFirstChild("Content")
	local grid = ui:Clear(content.Grid)
	local list = {}
	for id, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(resident) == "table" and wanted(resident) then
			table.insert(list, { Id = id, R = resident })
		end
	end
	table.sort(list, function(a: any, b: any): boolean
		if tab == "Working" then
			local ja, jb = jobOf(a.R) or "", jobOf(b.R) or ""
			if ja ~= jb then
				return ja < jb
			end
		end
		return (tonumber(string.match(a.Id, "%d+")) or 0) < (tonumber(string.match(b.Id, "%d+")) or 0)
	end)
	local stillThere = false
	for i, entry in list do
		local resident = entry.R
		local card = ui:Clone("Card")
		card.Name = entry.Id
		card.LayoutOrder = i
		ui:SetRarity(card, if resident.Tier == "Free" then "Common" else resident.Tier)
		local face = portrait()
		card.Portrait.Visible = face ~= nil
		if face then
			ui:SetSprite(card.Portrait, face)
		end
		card:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(resident.Name)
		local job = jobOf(resident)
		card.Sub.Text = (if resident.State == "Down" then "DOWN" elseif job then job else "Idle") .. `  ·  L{resident.Level}`
		card.Price.Visible = false
		card.Stamp.Visible = false
		ui:SetSprite(card.Lamp, if entry.Id == selected then "Lamp_Orange" else "Lamp_Off")
		card.Activated:Connect(function()
			selected = entry.Id
			fill()
		end)
		card.Parent = grid
		if entry.Id == selected then
			stillThere = true
		end
	end
	content.Empty.Visible = #list == 0
	if not stillThere then
		selected = if list[1] then list[1].Id else nil
		if selected then
			local first = grid:FindFirstChild(selected)
			if first then
				ui:SetSprite(first.Lamp, "Lamp_Orange")
			end
		end
	end
	if selected then
		showResident(selected)
	else
		showResident("")
	end
	local alive = 0
	for _, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(resident) == "table" and resident.State ~= "Dead" then
			alive += 1
		end
	end
	ui:SetHint(`{alive} residents in the bunker`)
end

function ResidentsController:Init(registry)
	ui = registry.UIController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
end

function ResidentsController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	ui:Register("Residents", {
		Title = "RESIDENTS",
		Subtitle = "STEADFAST SHELTER CO.  ·  PERSONNEL FILE",
		Tabs = {
			{ Id = "All", Label = "ALL", Icon = "Icon_Grid" },
			{ Id = "Working", Label = "WORKING", Icon = "Icon_Scrap" },
			{ Id = "Idle", Label = "IDLE", Icon = "Icon_Grid" },
			{ Id = "Hurt", Label = "HURT", Icon = "Icon_Shield" },
		},
		Layout = "Grid",
		Hint = "",
		OnOpen = function(p: Frame)
			page = p
			tab = "All"
			ui:SetFooterActions({
				{ Label = "Auto-Assign", OnPress = function()
					Remotes.FireServer("AutoAssign")
				end },
			})
			fill()
		end,
		OnTab = function(tabId: string, p: Frame)
			page = p
			tab = tabId
			fill()
		end,
		OnClose = function()
			page = nil
		end,
	})
	local pending = false
	replica:Changed("Residents"):Connect(function()
		if page and not pending then
			pending = true
			task.delay(0.3, function()
				pending = false
				fill()
			end)
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("Residents screen registered")
end

return ResidentsController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000068"><Properties><string name="Name">UIController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	UIController: The Frame (bible Section 18), the one layout every menu screen uses.

	The layout is StarterGui.Frame, built in Studio (studio/ui/Frame.lua) and given the
	AutoScale Lite pass; this controller only shows pages, clones templates and sets text and
	images. A screen registers once and opens by name:

		UIController:Register("Residents", {
			Title = "RESIDENTS",
			Subtitle = "STEADFAST SHELTER CO.  ·  PERSONNEL FILE",
			Tabs = { { Id = "All", Label = "ALL", Icon = "Icon_Grid" }, ... },  -- zone B, up to 7
			Layout = "Grid",       -- zone C: "Grid" (cards, always 1:1.25) or "List" (rows)
			Page = nil,            -- a page built for this screen under Cabinet.Pages; default: a clone of Templates.Page
			Docked = false,        -- the Command View: zone C shows the live bunker
			Hint = "...",          -- zone E
			OnOpen = function(page, args) end,
			OnTab = function(tabId, page) end,
			OnClose = function() end,
		})
		UIController:Open("Residents", args)

	Zone A shows the title and SetChips; zone D's main action is SetMainAction (the same place
	on every screen); zone E is SetHint and SetFooterActions. Code fills zones B to D with
	Clone("Card"), Clone("Row"), Clone("Section") and the Fill helpers.

	While a screen is open the mouse cursor is free, gameplay input is held off, and the HUD
	hides (HUDController listens to Opened and Closed). Keys: Backspace or the gamepad's B
	closes; Enter or Y presses the main action; L1 and R1 switch tabs.
]]

local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local UIContract = require(Shared.UIContract)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))

local log = Log.new("UIController")

export type Tab = { Id: string, Label: string, Icon: string? }
export type Screen = {
	Title: string,
	Subtitle: string?,
	Tabs: { Tab }?,
	Layout: string?,
	Page: string?,
	Docked: boolean?,
	Hint: string?,
	GamepadSelect: boolean?, -- false: no gamepad selection (the screen uses A itself)
	OnOpen: ((page: Frame, args: any) -> ())?,
	OnTab: ((tabId: string, page: Frame) -> ())?,
	OnClose: (() -> ())?,
}
export type MainAction = { Label: string, Price: string?, Icon: string?, Enabled: boolean?, OnPress: (() -> ())? }
export type Chip = { Icon: string, Text: string }
export type FooterAction = { Label: string, OnPress: () -> () }

local CLOSE_ACTION = "100Y_UIClose"
local MAIN_ACTION = "100Y_UIMain"
local TAB_ACTION = "100Y_UITab"
local PRIORITY = Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 20
local RARITIES = { Common = true, Rare = true, Epic = true, Legendary = true }

local UIController = {
	Name = "UIController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "CameraController" },
	Opened = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<string>,
	Closed = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<string>,
	TabChanged = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<string>,
}

local input: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local gui: ScreenGui? = nil
local screens: { [string]: Screen } = {}
local pages: { [string]: Frame } = {}
local current: string? = nil
local currentTab: string? = nil
local mainPress: (() -> ())? = nil
local tabButtons: { [string]: ImageButton } = {}
local footerConnections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}
local tabConnections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}

local function part(path: string): any
	assert(gui, "UIController: StarterGui.Frame is missing")
	local found = UIContract.Find(gui, path)
	assert(found, `UIController: Frame.{path} is missing (see Shared.UIContract)`)
	return found
end

local function clear(container: Instance)
	for _, child in container:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			child:Destroy()
		end
	end
end

local function disconnectAll(list: { RBXScriptConnection })
	for _, connection in list do
		connection:Disconnect()
	end
	table.clear(list)
end

local function keysText(screen: Screen): string
	local device = input:Device()
	local action = if mainPress then string.upper(part("Cabinet.MainAction.Content.Label").Text) else nil
	if device == "Gamepad" then
		local tabs = if screen.Tabs and #screen.Tabs > 1 then "     LB  RB  TABS" else ""
		return "B  CLOSE" .. (if action then `     Y  {action}` else "") .. tabs
	elseif device == "Keyboard" then
		return "BACKSPACE  CLOSE" .. (if action then `     ENTER  {action}` else "")
	end
	return ""
end

local function refreshKeys()
	if current then
		part("Cabinet.Footer.Keys").Text = keysText(screens[current])
	end
end

local function selectTab(id: string)
	if not current then
		return
	end
	local screen = screens[current]
	for tabId, button in tabButtons do
		local on = tabId == id
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(button, if on then "Tab_On" else "Tab_Off")
		local content = button:FindFirstChild("Content")
		if content then
			local icon = content:FindFirstChild("Icon") :: ImageLabel?
			local label = content:FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel?
			local color = if on then Color3.fromHex("#F2E6C9") else Color3.fromHex("#1B2A3A")
			if icon then
				icon.ImageColor3 = color
			end
			if label then
				label.TextColor3 = color
			end
		end
	end
	currentTab = id
	UIController.TabChanged:Fire(id)
	local page = pages[current]
	if screen.OnTab and page then
		task.spawn(screen.OnTab, id, page)
	end
end

local function stepTab(step: number)
	local screen = if current then screens[current] else nil
	if not screen or not screen.Tabs or #screen.Tabs < 2 then
		return
	end
	local index = 1
	for i, tab in screen.Tabs do
		if tab.Id == currentTab then
			index = i
		end
	end
	index = (index - 1 + step) % #screen.Tabs + 1
	selectTab(screen.Tabs[index].Id)
end

local function pageFor(name: string, screen: Screen): Frame
	local existing = pages[name]
	if existing and existing.Parent then
		return existing
	end
	local holder = part("Cabinet.Pages")
	local built = holder:FindFirstChild(screen.Page or name)
	local page: Frame
	if built and built:IsA("Frame") then
		page = built
	else
		page = UIController:Clone("Page") :: any
		page.Name = name
		page.Parent = holder
	end
	page.Visible = false
	pages[name] = page
	return page
end

local function bindKeys(on: boolean)
	if not on then
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(CLOSE_ACTION)
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(MAIN_ACTION)
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(TAB_ACTION)
		return
	end
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(CLOSE_ACTION, function(_, state)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			UIController:Close()
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, PRIORITY, Enum.KeyCode.Backspace, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonB)
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(MAIN_ACTION, function(_, state)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			UIController:PressMainAction()
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, PRIORITY, Enum.KeyCode.Return, Enum.KeyCode.KeypadEnter, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonY)
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(TAB_ACTION, function(_, state, inputObject)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			stepTab(if inputObject.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL1 then -1 else 1)
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, PRIORITY, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL1, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR1)
end

-- API -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function UIController:Register(name: string, screen: Screen)
	assert(not screens[name], `UIController: {name} is registered twice`)
	assert(screen.Title, `UIController: {name} has no title`)
	assert(not screen.Tabs or #screen.Tabs <= 7, `UIController: {name} has more than 7 tabs`)
	screens[name] = screen
end

function UIController:IsRegistered(name: string): boolean
	return screens[name] ~= nil
end

function UIController:Open(name: string, args: any?): boolean
	local screen = screens[name]
	if not screen or not gui then
		log:Warn("can't open %s: %s", name, if gui then "not registered" else "no Frame")
		return false
	end
	if current == name then
		return true
	end
	if current then
		UIController:Close()
	end
	local page = pageFor(name, screen)
	current = name
	gui.Enabled = true
	local docked = screen.Docked == true
	part("Dim").Visible = not docked
	part("Cabinet.Backplate").Visible = not docked
	part("Cabinet.DockPlates").Visible = docked
	part("Cabinet.TopBar.Title.Text").Text = string.upper(screen.Title)
	part("Cabinet.TopBar.Subtitle").Text = screen.Subtitle or "STEADFAST SHELTER CO."
	UIController:SetChips({})
	UIController:SetHint(screen.Hint or "")
	UIController:SetFooterActions({})
	UIController:SetMainAction(nil)
	local content = page:FindFirstChild("Content")
	if content then
		local layout = screen.Layout or "Grid"
		local grid = content:FindFirstChild("Grid")
		local rows = content:FindFirstChild("List")
		if grid and grid:IsA("GuiObject") then
			grid.Visible = layout == "Grid"
		end
		if rows and rows:IsA("GuiObject") then
			rows.Visible = layout == "List"
		end
	end
	-- zone B
	disconnectAll(tabConnections)
	table.clear(tabButtons)
	local rail = page:FindFirstChild("Tabs")
	if rail then
		clear(rail)
		for i, tab in screen.Tabs or {} do
			local button = UIController:Clone("Tab") :: ImageButton
			button.Name = tab.Id
			button.LayoutOrder = i
			local tabContent = button:FindFirstChild("Content") :: Frame
			local label = tabContent:FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel
			local icon = tabContent:FindFirstChild("Icon") :: ImageLabel
			label.Text = string.upper(tab.Label)
			if tab.Icon then
				KitRuntime.SetSprite(icon, tab.Icon)
			else
				icon.Visible = false
			end
			button.Parent = rail
			tabButtons[tab.Id] = button
			table.insert(tabConnections, button.Activated:Connect(function()
				selectTab(tab.Id)
			end))
		end
	end
	page.Visible = true
	input:Block("Frame", true)
	camera:FreeCursor("Frame", true)
	camera:SetAiming(false)
	bindKeys(true)
	if screen.OnOpen then
		local ok, err = pcall(screen.OnOpen, page, args)
		if not ok then
			log:Warn("%s OnOpen failed: %s", name, tostring(err))
		end
	end
	if screen.Tabs and #screen.Tabs > 0 then
		selectTab(screen.Tabs[1].Id)
	end
	refreshKeys()
	if input:Device() == "Gamepad" and screen.GamepadSelect ~= false then
		GuiService.SelectedObject = (if screen.Tabs and #screen.Tabs > 0 then tabButtons[screen.Tabs[1].Id] else nil)
			or part("Cabinet.TopBar.Close")
	end
	log:Debug("opened %s", name)
	UIController.Opened:Fire(name)
	return true
end

function UIController:Close()
	local name = current
	if not name or not gui then
		return
	end
	local screen = screens[name]
	local page = pages[name]
	if page then
		page.Visible = false
	end
	current = nil
	currentTab = nil
	mainPress = nil
	disconnectAll(tabConnections)
	disconnectAll(footerConnections)
	gui.Enabled = false
	bindKeys(false)
	input:Block("Frame", false)
	camera:FreeCursor("Frame", false)
	if GuiService.SelectedObject and GuiService.SelectedObject:IsDescendantOf(gui) then
		GuiService.SelectedObject = nil
	end
	if screen and screen.OnClose then
		task.spawn(screen.OnClose)
	end
	log:Debug("closed %s", name)
	UIController.Closed:Fire(name)
end

function UIController:IsOpen(): boolean
	return current ~= nil
end

function UIController:Current(): string?
	return current
end

function UIController:CurrentTab(): string?
	return currentTab
end

function UIController:Page(): Frame?
	return if current then pages[current] else nil
end

function UIController:SelectTab(id: string)
	if tabButtons[id] then
		selectTab(id)
	end
end

-- Zone D's main action (nil hides it). Enabled = false greys it out.
function UIController:SetMainAction(action: MainAction?)
	local button = part("Cabinet.MainAction") :: ImageButton
	if not action then
		button.Visible = false
		mainPress = nil
		refreshKeys()
		return
	end
	button.Visible = true
	part("Cabinet.MainAction.Content.Label").Text = string.upper(action.Label)
	local icon = part("Cabinet.MainAction.Content.Icon") :: ImageLabel
	local price = part("Cabinet.MainAction.Content.Price") :: TextLabel
	icon.Visible = action.Icon ~= nil
	if action.Icon then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(icon, action.Icon)
	end
	price.Text = action.Price or ""
	price.Visible = action.Price ~= nil
	KitRuntime.SetEnabled(button, action.Enabled ~= false)
	mainPress = if action.Enabled ~= false then action.OnPress else nil
	refreshKeys()
end

function UIController:PressMainAction()
	local press = mainPress
	if press and current then
		task.spawn(press)
	end
end

-- Zone A's chips (currencies or resources), right to left as listed.
function UIController:SetChips(chips: { Chip })
	local holder = part("Cabinet.TopBar.Chips")
	clear(holder)
	for i, chip in chips do
		local item = UIController:Clone("Chip")
		item.LayoutOrder = i
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(item:FindFirstChild("Icon") :: ImageLabel, chip.Icon)
		local amount = item:FindFirstChild("Amount") :: TextLabel
		amount.Text = chip.Text
		item.Parent = holder
	end
end

local noticeToken = 0
local restingHint: { Text: string, Color: Color3 }? = nil -- the screen's own hint, under a notice
local NOTICE_SECONDS = 4
local NOTICE_COLORS: { [string]: Color3 } = { Warning = Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E"), Danger = Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E") }

function UIController:SetHint(text: string)
	if restingHint then
		restingHint.Text = text -- a notice is showing: the hint comes back after it
	else
		part("Cabinet.Footer.Hint").Text = text
	end
end

-- A message in the footer (zone E) for a few seconds, then the screen's hint again: the HUD's
-- alerts while a screen hides the HUD (a refused proposal in the Command View).
function UIController:Notice(text: string, kind: string?)
	local hint = part("Cabinet.Footer.Hint")
	if not restingHint then
		restingHint = { Text = hint.Text, Color = hint.TextColor3 }
	end
	noticeToken += 1
	local token = noticeToken
	hint.Text = string.upper(text)
	hint.TextColor3 = NOTICE_COLORS[kind or ""] or (restingHint :: any).Color
	task.delay(NOTICE_SECONDS, function()
		local resting = restingHint
		if token == noticeToken and resting then
			hint.Text = resting.Text
			hint.TextColor3 = resting.Color
			restingHint = nil
		end
	end)
end

-- Zone E's secondary actions (filters, sort, back).
function UIController:SetFooterActions(actions: { FooterAction })
	disconnectAll(footerConnections)
	local holder = part("Cabinet.Footer.Actions")
	clear(holder)
	for i, action in actions do
		local button = UIController:Clone("FooterButton") :: ImageButton
		button.LayoutOrder = i
		local label = (button:FindFirstChild("Content") :: Frame):FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel
		label.Text = string.upper(action.Label)
		table.insert(footerConnections, button.Activated:Connect(function()
			task.spawn(action.OnPress)
		end))
		button.Parent = holder
	end
end

-- A visible copy of one of Frame.Templates (Page, Tab, Chip, Card, Row, Section, FooterButton).
function UIController:Clone(template: string): GuiObject
	local source = part("Templates." .. template)
	local copy = source:Clone() :: GuiObject
	copy.Visible = true
	return copy
end

function UIController:SetSprite(image: ImageLabel | ImageButton, name: string)
	KitRuntime.SetSprite(image, name)
end

-- A card, or a page's detail panel, in a rarity's colours (Common, Rare, Epic, Legendary).
function UIController:SetRarity(item: Instance, rarity: string)
	assert(RARITIES[rarity], `UIController: unknown rarity {rarity}`)
	local sprite = "Card_" .. rarity
	if item:IsA("ImageButton") or item:IsA("ImageLabel") then
		if item:GetAttribute("Sprite") and string.find(item:GetAttribute("Sprite") :: string, "^Card_") then
			KitRuntime.SetSprite(item, sprite)
		end
	end
	for _, name in { "Tag", "Hero" } do
		local child = item:FindFirstChild(name)
		if child and (child:IsA("ImageLabel") or child:IsA("ImageButton")) then
			KitRuntime.SetSprite(child, sprite)
		end
	end
end

-- Empties a container (zone B, C or D's Body) and returns it, for filling with clones.
function UIController:Clear(container: Instance): Instance
	clear(container)
	return container
end

function UIController:Gui(): ScreenGui?
	return gui
end

-- Lifecycle -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function UIController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	camera = registry.CameraController
end

function UIController:Start()
	local playerGui = Players.LocalPlayer:WaitForChild("PlayerGui")
	local found = playerGui:WaitForChild("Frame", 20)
	if not found or not found:IsA("ScreenGui") then
		log:Warn("no Frame ScreenGui in this place; menu screens can't open")
		return
	end
	gui = found
	found.Enabled = false
	KitRuntime.Watch(found)
	local close = part("Cabinet.TopBar.Close") :: ImageButton
	close.Activated:Connect(function()
		UIController:Close()
	end)
	local main = part("Cabinet.MainAction") :: ImageButton
	main.Activated:Connect(function()
		UIController:PressMainAction()
	end)
	input.DeviceChanged:Connect(function(device: string)
		refreshKeys()
		-- a gamepad selection would swallow Enter on a keyboard (it clicks the selected button)
		local selected = GuiService.SelectedObject
		if device ~= "Gamepad" and selected and selected:IsDescendantOf(found) then
			GuiService.SelectedObject = nil
		elseif device == "Gamepad" and current and not selected and screens[current].GamepadSelect ~= false then
			local first = next(tabButtons)
			GuiService.SelectedObject = if first then tabButtons[first] else part("Cabinet.TopBar.Close")
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("the Frame is ready")
end

return UIController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000069"><Properties><string name="Name">VoteController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	VoteController: what a vote looks like (bible Section 8): "a slim banner under the year clock
	shows who proposed what, the cost, the tally and a timer, with large yes and no buttons. It
	never blocks the screen. The proposed room appears as a ghost outline in the Command View. One
	chime plays when a vote opens, another when it passes." Run place only.

	* The telegram (StarterGui.Votes.VoteBanner, above The Frame, so a vote can be answered from
	  the Command View or any other screen) shows the live vote from the Votes collection
	  (VoteService):
	  * what, and its cost: "KITCHEN  ·  120 SCRAP", or what comes back: "TEAR DOWN KITCHEN  ·
	    50 SCRAP BACK";
	  * who, the tally and the time: "LANDON  ·  YES 2  ·  NO 1  ·  12 S", plus what it needs when
	    that isn't the usual more yes than no ("3 OF 4 MUST SAY YES"), and "1 WAITING";
	  * the timer strip running down;
	  * YES and NO. Your vote stays pressed in, and you can change it until the vote closes.
	  When a vote closes the telegram shows PASSED or FAILED and why, then the next vote.
	* On PC the mouse belongs to the camera: click the mouse wheel to free the cursor and click
	  the buttons (the HUD's rule). On a controller (Landon, Nov 8, 2026): tap Y for yes, hold Y
	  for no (HOLD_SECONDS). The Frame's screens use Y for their main action, so while your
	  ballot is still open Y votes on any screen (a binding above The Frame's); once you have
	  voted, Y changes your vote only outside the screens. The buttons show their key chips
	  whenever Y would vote, on a gamepad. Touch players tap the buttons.
	* Ghost outlines in the Command View for open proposals ("KITCHEN?") and for construction
	  sites ("KITCHEN 45%"; an upgrade on Nightmare: "LEVEL 2 45%"), from the Votes and Sites
	  collections.
	* The Command View's Propose (SetHandler for Build, Upgrade, Merge and TearDown) sends the
	  Propose remote. BuildService answers on the telegram, or with an alert when it refuses.
	* Chimes: SoundService.VoteOpen and SoundService.VotePassed, when they exist (Prompt 32's
	  audio).
]]

local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local SoundService = game:GetService("SoundService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))

local log = Log.new("VoteController")

local ACTIONS = { "Build", "Upgrade", "Merge", "TearDown" }
local RESULT_WITH_NEXT = 1.5 -- seconds a result stays when another vote is already live
local LEAF = Color3.fromHex("#6F9B4C")
local RUST = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B")
local INK = Color3.fromHex("#2A3B4C")

local VoteController = {
	Name = "VoteController",
	Dependencies = { "ReplicaController", "CommandViewController", "InputController" },
}

local HOLD_SECONDS = 0.5 -- a controller's Y held this long votes no; a shorter tap votes yes
local VOTE_NOW = "100Y_VoteNow" -- Y above The Frame's main action while your ballot is open
local VOTE_NOW_PRIORITY = Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 30

local replica: any = nil
local commandView: any = nil
local input: any = nil
local yDownAt: number? = nil -- when Y went down (a controller's vote)
local yHeld = false -- this press already voted no
local voteNowBound = false
local yVotes = false -- would Y vote right now (the key chips show)
local showKeys: () -> () -- below
local bindVoteNow: (pending: boolean) -> () -- below
local gui: ScreenGui? = nil
local banner: any = nil
local shownId: string? = nil -- the vote on the telegram
local shownStatus: string? = nil
local resultUntil = 0
local ghosts: { [string]: boolean } = {} -- the ghost ids this controller made
local missingChimes: { [string]: boolean } = {}

local function chime(name: string)
	local sound = SoundService:FindFirstChild(name)
	if sound and sound:IsA("Sound") then
		SoundService:PlayLocalSound(sound)
	elseif not missingChimes[name] then
		missingChimes[name] = true
		log:Debug("no SoundService.%s yet (the audio prompt adds it)", name)
	end
end

local function myBallot(vote: any): string?
	local ballots = vote.Ballots
	return if type(ballots) == "table" then ballots[tostring(Players.LocalPlayer.UserId)] else nil
end

-- The vote the telegram shows: a result just in, else the live vote.
local function pick(): (string?, any)
	local votes = replica:All("Votes")
	local shown = if shownId then votes[shownId] else nil
	if shown and (shown.Status == "Passed" or shown.Status == "Failed") and os.clock() < resultUntil then
		return shownId, shown
	end
	for id, vote in votes do
		if type(vote) == "table" and vote.Status == "Live" then
			return id, vote
		end
	end
	return nil, nil
end

local function waitingCount(): number
	local n = 0
	for _, vote in replica:All("Votes") do
		if type(vote) == "table" and vote.Status == "Queued" then
			n += 1
		end
	end
	return n
end

local function anotherLive(except: string?): boolean
	for id, vote in replica:All("Votes") do
		if id ~= except and type(vote) == "table" and vote.Status == "Live" then
			return true
		end
	end
	return false
end

local function render()
	if not banner then
		return
	end
	-- a vote that just closed: note when its result stops showing, and chime a pass
	if shownId then
		local current = replica:Get("Votes", shownId)
		local status = if type(current) == "table" then current.Status else nil
		if status ~= shownStatus and (status == "Passed" or status == "Failed") then
			resultUntil = os.clock() + (if anotherLive(shownId) then RESULT_WITH_NEXT else Config.Get("Tuning", "Votes").ResultSeconds)
			if status == "Passed" then
				chime("VotePassed")
			end
		end
		shownStatus = status
	end
	local id, vote = pick()
	if not id or not vote then
		banner.Visible = false
		shownId, shownStatus = nil, nil
		yVotes = false
		bindVoteNow(false)
		showKeys()
		return
	end
	if id ~= shownId then
		shownId, shownStatus = id, vote.Status
		if vote.Status == "Live" then
			chime("VoteOpen")
		end
	end
	banner.Visible = true
	-- line 1: what and what it costs; line 2: who, the tally, the time and what it needs
	local cost = if type(vote.Cost) == "string" and vote.Cost ~= "" and vote.Cost ~= "FREE" then `  ·  {vote.Cost}`
		elseif type(vote.Refund) == "string" then `  ·  {vote.Refund} BACK`
		else ""
	banner.Proposal.Text = `{vote.Title}{cost}`
	local yes, no = banner.Yes, banner.No
	local fill = banner.Timer.Fill
	if vote.Status == "Live" then
		local left = math.max(0, (vote.EndsAt or 0) - workspace:GetServerTimeNow())
		local waiting = waitingCount()
		local need = if vote.Rule ~= "MoreYes" then `  ·  {vote.Need}` else "" -- "more yes than no" is the usual rule
		banner.Tally.Text = `{vote.ProposerName}  ·  YES {vote.Yes}  ·  NO {vote.No}  ·  {math.ceil(left)} S{need}`
			.. (if waiting > 0 then `  ·  {waiting} WAITING` else "")
		banner.Tally.TextColor3 = INK
		fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(math.clamp(left / math.max(vote.Seconds or 1, 1), 0, 1), 1)
		local ballot = myBallot(vote)
		bindVoteNow(ballot == nil)
		-- Y votes while the ballot is open, and outside the screens afterwards (to change it)
		yVotes = ballot == nil or not input:IsBlocked()
		showKeys()
		KitRuntime.SetEnabled(yes, true)
		KitRuntime.SetEnabled(no, true)
		KitRuntime.SetLatched(yes, ballot == "Yes")
		KitRuntime.SetLatched(no, ballot == "No")
	else
		banner.Tally.Text = tostring(vote.Result or vote.Status)
		banner.Tally.TextColor3 = if vote.Status == "Passed" then LEAF else RUST
		fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0, 1)
		KitRuntime.SetLatched(yes, false)
		KitRuntime.SetLatched(no, false)
		KitRuntime.SetEnabled(yes, false)
		KitRuntime.SetEnabled(no, false)
		bindVoteNow(false)
		yVotes = false
		showKeys()
	end
end

local function cast(ballot: string)
	local id, vote = pick()
	if id and vote and vote.Status == "Live" then
		Remotes.FireServer("CastVote", id, ballot)
	end
end

-- Ghost outlines in the Command View: open proposals and construction sites.
local function syncGhosts()
	local want: { [string]: { any } } = {}
	for id, vote in replica:All("Votes") do
		local subject = if type(vote) == "table" then vote.Subject else nil
		if type(subject) == "table" and (vote.Status == "Live" or vote.Status == "Queued") then
			want["vote:" .. id] = { subject.Floor, subject.Column, subject.Span, subject.Label }
		end
	end
	for id, site in replica:All("Sites") do
		if type(site) == "table" then
			local info = Config.Find("Rooms", site.Type)
			local name = if site.Kind == "Upgrade" then `LEVEL {site.Level}`
				elseif info then string.upper(info.Name)
				else tostring(site.Type)
			want["site:" .. id] = { site.Floor, site.Column, site.Span, `{name} {math.floor((site.Progress or 0) * 100)}%` }
		end
	end
	for key, g in want do
		if ghosts[key] then
			commandView:SetGhostLabel(key, g[4])
		else
			commandView:ShowGhost(key, g[1], g[2], g[3], g[4])
			ghosts[key] = true
		end
	end
	for key in ghosts do
		if not want[key] then
			commandView:HideGhost(key)
			ghosts[key] = nil
		end
	end
end

function VoteController:State(): { [string]: any }
	local id, vote = pick()
	return {
		Shown = id,
		Visible = banner ~= nil and banner.Visible,
		Proposal = if banner then banner.Proposal.Text else nil,
		Tally = if banner then banner.Tally.Text else nil,
		Mine = if vote then myBallot(vote) else nil,
		Ghosts = (function()
			local keys = {}
			for key in ghosts do
				table.insert(keys, key)
			end
			table.sort(keys)
			return table.concat(keys, ",")
		end)(),
	}
end

-- The key chips show on a gamepad while Y would vote (PC clicks, touch taps).
showKeys = function()
	if not banner then
		return
	end
	local visible = yVotes and input:Device() == "Gamepad"
	for _, name in { "Yes", "No" } do
		local key = banner[name]:FindFirstChild("Key")
		if key and key.Visible ~= visible then
			key.Visible = visible
		end
	end
end

-- A controller's Y: a tap votes yes; held for HOLD_SECONDS it votes no (once per press).
local function yBegan()
	yDownAt = os.clock()
	yHeld = false
end

local function yEnded()
	if yDownAt and not yHeld then
		cast("Yes")
	end
	yDownAt = nil
	yHeld = false
end

local function checkHold()
	if yDownAt and not yHeld and os.clock() - yDownAt >= HOLD_SECONDS then
		yHeld = true
		cast("No")
	end
end

-- While your ballot is open (and while Y is still held), Y is bound above The Frame's main action.
bindVoteNow = function(pending: boolean)
	local want = pending or yDownAt ~= nil
	if want == voteNowBound then
		return
	end
	voteNowBound = want
	if want then
		ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(VOTE_NOW, function(_name, state: Enum.UserInputState): Enum.ContextActionResult
			if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
				yBegan()
			elseif state == Enum.UserInputState.End or state == Enum.UserInputState.Cancel then
				yEnded()
			end
			return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
		end, false, VOTE_NOW_PRIORITY, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonY)
	else
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(VOTE_NOW)
	end
end

function VoteController:Init(registry)
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	commandView = registry.CommandViewController
	input = registry.InputController
end

function VoteController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	for _, action in ACTIONS do
		commandView:SetHandler(action, function(choice: any)
			local detail = if action == "Build" then (choice.RoomType or "") elseif action == "Merge" then (choice.Other or "") else ""
			Remotes.FireServer("Propose", action, choice.Floor, choice.Column, detail)
		end)
	end
	replica:Changed("Votes"):Connect(syncGhosts)
	replica:Changed("Sites"):Connect(syncGhosts)
	syncGhosts()

	local found = Players.LocalPlayer:WaitForChild("PlayerGui"):WaitForChild("Votes", 20)
	if not found or not found:IsA("ScreenGui") then
		log:Warn("no Votes ScreenGui in this place: the vote telegram can't show")
		return
	end
	gui = found
	KitRuntime.Watch(found)
	banner = found:FindFirstChild("VoteBanner")
	if not banner then
		log:Warn("the Votes ScreenGui has no VoteBanner")
		return
	end
	banner.Yes.Activated:Connect(function()
		cast("Yes")
	end)
	banner.No.Activated:Connect(function()
		cast("No")
	end)
	input:On("Vote", yBegan, yEnded)
	input.DeviceChanged:Connect(showKeys)
	showKeys()
	local elapsed = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function(dt: number)
		checkHold()
		elapsed += dt
		if elapsed >= 0.1 then
			elapsed = 0
			render()
		end
	end)
	render()
	log:Debug("vote telegram ready")
end

return VoteController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item></Item><Item class="Folder" referent="RBX0000006F"><Properties><string name="Name">Lib</string></Properties><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000006B"><Properties><string name="Name">Fade</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	Fade: see-through world parts on this client only, shared by the camera (walls and
	furniture between the camera and the character) and the Command View (front walls).

	Each source asks for an amount per part (0 opaque, 1 hidden); a part shows the largest ask,
	eased over `seconds`, through BasePart.LocalTransparencyModifier, which is local to this
	client and never replicates. Parts that leave the game drop out by themselves.

		Fade.Set(part, "Camera", 0.8)
		Fade.Clear(part, "Camera")
		Fade.ClearSource("Camera")
]]

local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")

local Fade = {}

local DEFAULT_SECONDS = 0.12

local asks: { [BasePart]: { [string]: number } } = {}
local shown: { [BasePart]: number } = {}
local seconds = DEFAULT_SECONDS
local connection: RBXScriptConnection? = nil

local function target(part: BasePart): number
	local best = 0
	for _, amount in asks[part] or {} do
		best = math.max(best, amount)
	end
	return best
end

local function step(dt: number)
	local rate = if seconds > 0 then dt / seconds else 1
	local busy = false
	for part, current in shown do
		if part.Parent == nil then
			shown[part] = nil
			asks[part] = nil
			continue
		end
		local goal = target(part)
		local nextValue = if current < goal then math.min(current + rate, goal) else math.max(current - rate, goal)
		if nextValue ~= current then
			part.LocalTransparencyModifier = nextValue
		end
		if nextValue <= 0 and goal <= 0 then
			shown[part] = nil
			asks[part] = nil
		else
			shown[part] = nextValue
			busy = true
		end
	end
	if not busy and connection then
		connection:Disconnect()
		connection = nil
	end
end

local function wake()
	if not connection then
		connection = RunService.RenderStepped:Connect(step)
	end
end

-- How long a fade in or out takes (the camera sets this from Tuning.Camera.FadeSeconds).
function Fade.SetSeconds(value: number)
	seconds = math.max(0, value)
end

function Fade.Set(part: BasePart, source: string, amount: number)
	local list = asks[part]
	if not list then
		list = {}
		asks[part] = list
	end
	list[source] = math.clamp(amount, 0, 1)
	if shown[part] == nil then
		shown[part] = part.LocalTransparencyModifier
	end
	wake()
end

function Fade.Clear(part: BasePart, source: string)
	local list = asks[part]
	if list then
		list[source] = nil
	end
	if shown[part] ~= nil then
		wake()
	end
end

-- Drops every ask a source made (when the camera stops, or the Command View closes).
function Fade.ClearSource(source: string)
	for part, list in asks do
		if list[source] ~= nil then
			list[source] = nil
			wake()
		end
	end
end

-- The parts a source is fading now (DevTools).
function Fade.Count(source: string?): number
	local count = 0
	for _, list in asks do
		if source == nil or list[source] ~= nil then
			count += 1
		end
	end
	return count
end

return Fade
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000006C"><Properties><string name="Name">KitRuntime</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	Lib.KitRuntime: keeps the UI kit right on every screen (bible Section 18).

	* 9-slice corners: kit sprites are drawn at twice their 1080p size, so a sliced image's
	  SliceScale is 0.5 x height / 1080 (times its SliceMul attribute, if any).
	* Strokes and scroll bars are pixels, so their 1080p sizes (BaseThickness, BaseScrollBar
	  attributes) follow the screen height too: the StrokeScaler of the AutoScale Lite rules.
	* Push-buttons: the builder writes RectUp, RectDown and optionally RectHover and
	  RectDisabled. The pressed sprite shows while the button is held, and its Content frame
	  sinks a little, like a real cap.

	Watch(gui) does all of this for a ScreenGui now, for anything cloned into it later, and
	again whenever its size changes. SetSprite points an image at a kit sprite and keeps a
	builder's crop. SetEnabled greys a button out.
]]

local UIKit = require(script.Parent.UIKit)

local KitRuntime = {}

local SINK = 0.06 -- how far a pressed button's Content moves down (of its height)

local hooked: { [Instance]: boolean } = setmetatable({}, { __mode = "k" }) :: any

local function heightOf(gui: Instance): number
	local h = 0
	if gui:IsA("LayerCollector") then
		local layer: any = gui
		h = layer.AbsoluteSize.Y
	end
	if h <= 0 then
		local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
		h = if camera then camera.ViewportSize.Y else 1080
	end
	return math.max(h, 1)
end

local function scaleOne(o: Instance, k: number)
	local item: any = o
	if (o:IsA("ImageLabel") or o:IsA("ImageButton")) and item.ScaleType == Enum.ScaleType.Slice then
		local mul = o:GetAttribute("SliceMul")
		item.SliceScale = 0.5 * k * (if type(mul) == "number" then mul else 1)
	elseif o:IsA("UIStroke") then
		local base = o:GetAttribute("BaseThickness")
		if type(base) == "number" then
			item.Thickness = base * k
		end
	elseif o:IsA("ScrollingFrame") then
		local base = o:GetAttribute("BaseScrollBar")
		if type(base) == "number" then
			item.ScrollBarThickness = math.max(2, math.round(base * k))
		end
	end
end

local function rect(button: Instance, state: string): Vector2?
	local value = button:GetAttribute("Rect" .. state)
	return if typeof(value) == "Vector2" then value else nil
end

local function show(button: ImageButton, state: string)
	local r = rect(button, state) or rect(button, "Up")
	if r then
		button.ImageRectOffset = r
	end
	local content = button:FindFirstChild("Content")
	if content and content:IsA("GuiObject") then
		local home = content:GetAttribute("Home")
		if typeof(home) ~= "UDim2" then
			home = content.Position
			content:SetAttribute("Home", home)
		end
		local rest: UDim2 = home :: any
		content.Position = if state == "Down" then rest + UDim2.fromScale(0, SINK) else rest
	end
end

local function hook(button: ImageButton)
	if hooked[button] or not rect(button, "Up") or not rect(button, "Down") then
		return
	end
	hooked[button] = true
	local over = false
	local function settle()
		if button:GetAttribute("Disabled") == true then
			show(button, "Disabled")
		elseif button:GetAttribute("Latched") == true then
			show(button, "Down") -- held in: a vote cast, a toggle on
		else
			show(button, if over and rect(button, "Hover") then "Hover" else "Up")
		end
	end
	button.MouseButton1Down:Connect(function()
		if button:GetAttribute("Disabled") ~= true then
			show(button, "Down")
		end
	end)
	button.MouseButton1Up:Connect(settle)
	button.MouseEnter:Connect(function()
		over = true
		settle()
	end)
	button.MouseLeave:Connect(function()
		over = false
		settle()
	end)
	button:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Disabled"):Connect(settle)
	button:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Latched"):Connect(settle)
	settle()
end

-- Applies the kit's runtime rules to a ScreenGui. Returns a function that stops watching.
function KitRuntime.Watch(gui: Instance): () -> ()
	local function factor(): number
		return heightOf(gui) / 1080
	end
	local function applyAll()
		local k = factor()
		for _, o in gui:GetDescendants() do
			scaleOne(o, k)
		end
	end
	for _, o in gui:GetDescendants() do
		if o:IsA("ImageButton") then
			hook(o)
		end
	end
	applyAll()
	local connections = {
		gui:GetPropertyChangedSignal("AbsoluteSize"):Connect(applyAll),
		gui.DescendantAdded:Connect(function(o: Instance)
			scaleOne(o, factor())
			if o:IsA("ImageButton") then
				hook(o)
			end
		end),
	}
	return function()
		for _, connection in connections do
			connection:Disconnect()
		end
	end
end

-- Points an image at a kit sprite. An image the builder cropped (a card's rarity tag, say)
-- keeps its crop inside the new sprite.
function KitRuntime.SetSprite(image: ImageLabel | ImageButton, name: string)
	local sprite = UIKit.Sprites[name]
	assert(sprite, `KitRuntime: no sprite {name}`)
	local item: any = image
	item.Image = sprite.image
	local crop = image:GetAttribute("Crop")
	if typeof(crop) == "Vector2" then
		item.ImageRectOffset = sprite.offset + crop
	else
		item.ImageRectOffset = sprite.offset
		item.ImageRectSize = sprite.size
		if sprite.slice then
			item.ScaleType = Enum.ScaleType.Slice
			item.SliceCenter = sprite.slice
		else
			item.ScaleType = Enum.ScaleType.Stretch
		end
	end
	image:SetAttribute("Sprite", name)
	local gui = image:FindFirstAncestorWhichIsA("LayerCollector")
	scaleOne(image, heightOf(gui or image) / 1080)
end

-- Greys a push-button out (its Disabled sprite when it has one) or brings it back.
function KitRuntime.SetEnabled(button: ImageButton, on: boolean)
	button:SetAttribute("Disabled", if on then nil else true)
	if not hooked[button] then
		show(button, if on then "Up" else "Disabled")
	end
end

-- Holds a push-button in (a vote cast, a toggle that is on) until released.
function KitRuntime.SetLatched(button: ImageButton, on: boolean)
	button:SetAttribute("Latched", if on then true else nil)
end

function KitRuntime.IsEnabled(button: Instance): boolean
	return button:GetAttribute("Disabled") ~= true
end

return KitRuntime
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000006D"><Properties><string name="Name">Movement</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	Movement: the local character's walk speed, from everything that changes it, so no two
	controllers fight over Humanoid.WalkSpeed (aiming slows it, sprinting speeds it up and a
	downed player crawls; bible Section 9).

		Movement.Set(reason, multiplier?)  -- a multiplier on the base speed; nil removes it
		Movement.Override(reason, speed?)  -- a fixed speed that wins over the multipliers (the
		                                    -- slowest override wins); nil removes it
		Movement.Speed(): number
		Movement.Apply()                   -- after the character changes

	The base speed is StarterPlayer.CharacterWalkSpeed.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local StarterPlayer = game:GetService("StarterPlayer")

local Movement = {}

local multipliers: { [string]: number } = {}
local overrides: { [string]: number } = {}

function Movement.Speed(): number
	local slowest: number? = nil
	for _, speed in overrides do
		slowest = if slowest then math.min(slowest, speed) else speed
	end
	if slowest then
		return slowest
	end
	local speed = StarterPlayer.CharacterWalkSpeed
	for _, multiplier in multipliers do
		speed *= multiplier
	end
	return speed
end

function Movement.Apply()
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	if humanoid then
		local speed = Movement.Speed()
		if math.abs(humanoid.WalkSpeed - speed) > 1e-3 then
			humanoid.WalkSpeed = speed
		end
	end
end

function Movement.Set(reason: string, multiplier: number?)
	if multipliers[reason] == multiplier then
		return
	end
	multipliers[reason] = multiplier
	Movement.Apply()
end

function Movement.Override(reason: string, speed: number?)
	if overrides[reason] == speed then
		return
	end
	overrides[reason] = speed
	Movement.Apply()
end

function Movement.Has(reason: string): boolean
	return multipliers[reason] ~= nil or overrides[reason] ~= nil
end

return Movement
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000006E"><Properties><string name="Name">UIKit</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
